// Generated by scripts/reading/build-planet-text.py from docs/redesign/drafts/*-planets-*.md.
// Reading page only ("you" voice). The shared library in lib/interpretations stays third person
// for celebrity and /interpretations pages. Missing keys fall back to the library text.

export const YOU_IN_SIGN: Record<string, string> = {
  "CHIRON_Aquarius": "Your tender spot is fitting in. You were likely the outsider early, kept at the edge of the circle, and you still feel alien sometimes, or detach to stay safe. It grows into deep empathy for anyone excluded, and a gift for championing people who stand on the margins the way you once did.",
  "CHIRON_Aries": "Your sore spot is the right to exist boldly. Early on, taking up space or simply going first may have felt not quite allowed, so now you either hold back or push too hard. The other side of that same nerve is your gift: you know what it costs to claim yourself, and you're uncannily good at helping other people find the courage to step forward.",
  "CHIRON_Cancer": "Belonging is where it aches. Care may have been absent or unreliable early on, and home felt tender and uncertain. You either long for security or guard your heart heavily. Because you felt the lack, you have an extraordinary capacity to nurture others and build them the belonging you once had to go without.",
  "CHIRON_Capricorn": "You learned early that achievement earned acceptance, as if you only mattered for what you produced. Relentless ambition and a fear of never being enough are the echoes. What it built in you is structure: a talent for mentoring and steadying people, giving them the recognition and solid ground you once missed.",
  "CHIRON_Gemini": "Your voice is the tender place. Maybe nobody listened when you were small, or not clever enough, with your words never quite landing, and now you doubt your own mind or dread speaking up. You also know personally what it is to feel unheard, and that becomes a real gift for language and for helping other people find and trust their voices.",
  "CHIRON_Leo": "Being seen is your sore spot. Your early wish to shine, or a bid for attention, may have met rejection or embarrassment, and now you fear the spotlight or hunger for it, sometimes both. The warmth survived anyway, and it gives you a gift for drawing out other people's light and helping them shine the way that once felt unsafe for you.",
  "CHIRON_Libra": "Relationships are where you're tender. Early on you felt unchosen, or unsure you were worth loving; now rejection scares you, or you give too much. Out of that ache comes a deep understanding of what makes connection work, and a real talent for helping others find the love and balance that once felt out of reach.",
  "CHIRON_Pisces": "Boundaries and faith are where it hurts. Too open to the pain of the world, or disillusioned early, you can drift into escape or feel lost. The compassion that came out of it is profound. You know what it is to long for grace, and you can offer some to other people.",
  "CHIRON_Sagittarius": "Meaning is the ache. A faith or a set of beliefs may have failed you early, leaving the search for truth feeling raw. Cynicism and restless spiritual hunger both grow from that. From that loss comes hard won wisdom, and you help others find a meaning they can actually live by.",
  "CHIRON_Scorpio": "Your sore spot is power and trust. An early betrayal, loss or feeling of powerlessness cut deep, leaving you guarded about intimacy or tangled up in control. The depth it opened is your gift: you can walk with people through their darkest stretches without flinching, because you've been through one yourself.",
  "CHIRON_Taurus": "For you it's worth and security: an early sense of not having enough, or not being enough, with the ground never quite solid. Money worries or trouble feeling deserving follow from it. From the same soil grows a lived understanding of how real security works, and you're able to help others build a steady sense of their own value.",
  "CHIRON_Virgo": "You know the feeling of not being good enough: an early sense that only flawless counted, with you forever falling short. It shows up as harsh self criticism or anxious perfectionism. The compassion it taught you is real. You have a healer's eye for what needs mending, and you can help people accept themselves as whole, unfinished and worthy at once.",
  "JUPITER_Aquarius": "You grow through ideals, community and a vision aimed at the future. Progress and the good of the many are what you believe in, and luck flows to you through networks and causes. You can be generous toward humanity and cool toward the one person in front of you. Let the big vision reach the people actually nearby.",
  "JUPITER_Aries": "You grow by leaping first and trusting the path to appear. Self belief and a taste for fresh starts are your kind of faith, and luck tends to favor you when you move. Enthusiasm can launch a dozen ventures and finish none of them. Pair the courage to begin with the patience to see one thing through, and the luck compounds.",
  "JUPITER_Cancer": "Jupiter is exalted in Cancer, at its most generous, and you grow through care, home and open hearted support for other people. Belonging is your faith, and luck flows through family and the bonds that hold. You give past every boundary if nobody stops you. Real care leaves room for the other person to stand on their own.",
  "JUPITER_Capricorn": "Capricorn is Jupiter's fall, and your growth is slow, disciplined and earned, not given. Realism keeps your optimism in check, you trust what you've built, and luck comes through patience and work. You can shrink hope down to what's already proven. Some risks are worth taking before all the evidence is in.",
  "JUPITER_Gemini": "Your growth comes through ideas and learning, spread across many subjects. Jupiter is weak in Gemini by Lilly's rules, the big picture planet in the sign of small facts, and you feel it as breadth over depth. You're curious, well connected and lucky in conversation. Let curiosity settle long enough to turn information into understanding, and you become the expert instead of the trivia champion.",
  "JUPITER_Leo": "You grow through your heart: creativity, play and generosity worn proudly. You believe life is meant to be enjoyed and shared, and luck likes warm, bold people like you. Sometimes the grandeur overreaches into showing off. Your generosity is best as a gift, not a performance.",
  "JUPITER_Libra": "You grow through partnership, fairness and the real pleasure of meeting people well. You believe in what people can do together, and luck flows to you through alliances and grace. You can overaccommodate to keep the peace. Hold your own center while you reach warmly toward the other person.",
  "JUPITER_Pisces": "Jupiter is Pisces' traditional ruler (modern astrology gives it Neptune), and you grow through compassion, faith and a sense of something boundless and bigger than you. Your belief is oceanic and intuitive, and luck seems to arrive when you stop forcing it. Watch for faith drifting into escape or wishful thinking. Anchor all that compassion in something real enough to act on.",
  "JUPITER_Sagittarius": "Jupiter rules Sagittarius, so you're at home: you grow through meaning, travel and the restless search for a wider truth. Faith is your native element, expansive and contagious, and luck loves a seeker. Your belief can harden into a sermon, and your promises can outrun your calendar. Hold your beliefs with the same curiosity that made them worth having.",
  "JUPITER_Scorpio": "You grow through depth: facing what's hidden and coming out larger. Your faith is hard won and rests in the power of starting over, and luck favors you because you aren't afraid to dig. In the deep places, your appetite can reach for power and control. Real abundance comes through letting go as much as through will.",
  "JUPITER_Taurus": "You grow slowly and solidly, building the kind of plenty you can touch and keep. You trust what accumulates, and luck comes to you through patience and good sense. A generous appetite for comfort can tip into too much of everything. Enough, really felt, is its own kind of wealth.",
  "JUPITER_Virgo": "Your growth comes through the small and the useful, refining more than reaching. Virgo is one of Jupiter's detriments, big meaning stuck with fine print, so your faith is modest and earned through good work, and luck favors your diligence. The big picture can shrink into nitpicking and worry. Lift your eyes from the details now and then; the larger meaning is worth seeing.",
  "MARS_Aquarius": "You act on principle. Your drive is independent and contrarian, powered by ideas, and you'll fight harder for the cause and the future than for yourself. Your wants are cool and a little detached. Watch for resisting on reflex, pushing against something simply because it's expected. Choose your fights for conviction, not for the pleasure of not fitting in.",
  "MARS_Aries": "Mars rules Aries, so your drive comes out pure: direct, fast and immediate, acting before second thoughts can slow you down. You want things simply and you meet a fight head on. You're at your strongest at the moment you start. Sometimes you charge before you've picked a direction, or take a fight for the heat of it. The strongest move is sometimes the one you haven't made yet.",
  "MARS_Cancer": "Mars has its fall in Cancer, and your drive moves sideways rather than straight on: tidal, emotional, tied up with feeling. You protect more than you conquer, and you're fiercest when home or family is threatened. Anger tends to leak out as moodiness instead of being said. Name what you want out loud; it's kinder than seething.",
  "MARS_Capricorn": "Capricorn is where Mars is exalted, at its most effective, and your drive is disciplined, strategic and built for the long climb. You spend energy with patience and almost no waste, and you win by outlasting. Your ambition is controlled and real. The climb was meant to serve your life, not consume it, so remember to rest, and let everyone else rest too.",
  "MARS_Gemini": "Your drive runs through your mind: words, debate, quick moves on several fronts at once. Your wants are restless and easy to redirect, and you fight with your tongue. You may start more than you finish and argue more than you act. Aim all that energy at one target long enough to actually land it.",
  "MARS_Leo": "You act with pride. Your drive is confident, dramatic and generous, and you show your strength instead of hiding it. You fight for honor and want your effort seen. Watch where the energy goes: into being admired, or into the goal? Let the work matter more than the applause, and the applause tends to come anyway.",
  "MARS_Libra": "Your drive runs through fairness and the wish to keep the peace. Mars is in detriment in Libra, the sign of manners, so you're slow to push and quick to see the other side, and you'd rather avoid a fight where you can. You may want agreement before you act, then resent what you didn't claim. Some things have to be asked for directly.",
  "MARS_Pisces": "Your drive is diffuse and intuitive, hard to aim in a straight line. You move by feeling and current rather than force, and you can be unsure what you actually want. You tend to slip around a fight instead of facing it. Unspent, the energy can drain into avoidance or self sacrifice. Give it a channel real enough to carry it somewhere: art, care, a cause you can see.",
  "MARS_Sagittarius": "You act on conviction. Your drive is enthusiastic and restless, aimed at the horizon, fighting for what you believe and for the freedom to roam. You get bored easily and chase the next bigger thing. Grand campaigns can get dropped when the novelty fades. Pick one quest and stay with it long enough to see it through.",
  "MARS_Scorpio": "Mars is Scorpio's traditional ruler (modern astrology adds Pluto), and your drive is intense, strategic and relentless, moving quietly toward one deep aim. You want things totally and rarely show it. You fight patiently, and when you finish a fight, it stays finished. Your will doesn't let go easily, of goals or grudges. Learn the difference between enduring for a purpose and simply refusing to release.",
  "MARS_Taurus": "You're slow to get going and nearly impossible to stop once you do. Lilly counts Taurus against Mars, because the planet of the quick strike is sitting in the sign of patience, and you work that way: endurance over speed, the long siege over the raid. Your wants are steady and physical. Watch for pushing something long past its use simply because stopping feels like losing. Knowing when to put the weight down is a strength too.",
  "MARS_Virgo": "You act with precision. Your drive is methodical and efficient, aimed at doing the thing exactly right, and you win by preparing better than anyone. Your energy goes into useful work and visible skill. It can also go into fault finding, perfecting and worrying over details. Let good work ship before it's polished into paralysis.",
  "MERCURY_Aquarius": "You think in systems. Your mind runs on patterns, principles and the odd angle nobody else considered, and you like to step back and see the whole structure from above. You come across original, objective and a little cool. Your blind spot is a fixed conclusion: being so proud of thinking differently that you hold an idea because it's unusual, not because it's true.",
  "MERCURY_Aries": "You think at a sprint. Ideas arrive already decided, and you're answering before the room has finished the question. You say things plainly and you'd rather be wrong out loud than vague. Your mind is sharpest in the moment of engagement, less so after a week of mulling. One deliberate pause, now and then, makes a quick mind like yours nearly unbeatable, because your first thought isn't always your final one.",
  "MERCURY_Cancer": "You think through feeling. Ideas come wrapped in mood and memory, and you reason from what something feels like as much as from what it is. You choose words for how they'll land, and you remember the emotional texture of conversations years later. It makes you a gentle, intuitive communicator. The tricky part is telling a feeling from a fact, especially when the truth hurts and the comfortable version is right there.",
  "MERCURY_Capricorn": "You think in structures. Your ideas are organized, strategic and aimed at something that will actually stand, and you don't waste words. You plan in long arcs and rarely lose the thread. Your imagination is on a short leash, and you can dismiss an idea simply because it hasn't proven itself yet. Not every useful thought shows up already wearing a suit.",
  "MERCURY_Gemini": "Mercury rules Gemini, so your mind is in its element: quick, fluent and endlessly curious, connecting things that don't obviously belong together. You can talk in any register and you have a real gift for words and patterns. You also have about forty open tabs. You generate more ideas than you finish, and your best work comes when you follow one thread all the way down.",
  "MERCURY_Leo": "You think with flair. Your ideas come out warm, confident and meant to be heard, with your whole personality behind them. You're persuasive, expressive and a little theatrical, and you usually win the room. Arguments are where you get caught: defending a position because it's yours, not because it's right. Changing your mind in public costs you nothing. It might even win you a bigger room.",
  "MERCURY_Libra": "You think in pairs. Every idea gets weighed against its opposite, and you reason by comparison, fairness and the view from both sides. You're diplomatic, easy to agree with and genuinely good at seeing what the other side gets right. Then there's the verdict that never quite arrives. Weighing forever isn't the same as being fair, and sometimes the fair thing is to decide.",
  "MERCURY_Pisces": "Pisces is Mercury's weakest sign, both detriment and fall, which mostly means your mind doesn't work in straight lines. You think in images, impressions and hunches, and you often know something without being able to say how. You speak poetically and can be hard to pin down. The gift is real originality. Trust your intuition, and build just enough structure to carry it back to everyone else.",
  "MERCURY_Sagittarius": "Lilly counts Sagittarius against Mercury, and you'll recognize the trade: you grasp the big picture instantly and lose patience with the fine print. You speak frankly and love a sweeping statement. You care about meaning more than mechanics, the forest more than the trees. You're often right about the whole and careless about the parts, so slow down long enough to check the details you'd rather skip.",
  "MERCURY_Scorpio": "You think beneath the surface. You distrust the obvious answer and dig for the motive, the secret, the thing nobody's saying. You speak deliberately and often hold back until you have the whole picture, and few people investigate as relentlessly as you. Suspicion can become your default setting, though. Not every plain surface is hiding something, and some people mean exactly what they say.",
  "MERCURY_Taurus": "You think slowly and for keeps. An idea gets chewed, tested against something real, and adopted only once it holds weight. You talk plainly and hate being rushed, and once your mind is made up, it tends to stay that way. You trust what you can touch over what merely sounds clever. Stay open to the better argument when it comes, because stubborn and convinced feel exactly the same from the inside.",
  "MERCURY_Virgo": "Mercury both rules Virgo and is exalted there, so your mind is at its sharpest: precise, analytical and gifted at catching the detail everyone else skims past. You choose your words carefully and they're usually useful. Few people take a problem apart as cleanly as you do. The risk is a critic that never clocks out, picking at everything, you included. Good enough is sometimes exactly enough.",
  "MOON_Aquarius": "You process feelings at a cool distance, through ideas and observation, a step back from the heat. Space and independence help you feel safe, and so does belonging to something bigger than one close bond. You're friendly to everyone and warmer toward humanity than toward intimacy. Watch that the step back doesn't become a wall. Come close enough to your own feelings to be touched by them.",
  "MOON_Aries": "Your feelings arrive at full volume and want out right now. Sitting with an emotion feels like waiting in line, so you do something with it instead: say it, fix it, go for a run. You're honest, quick to flare and quick to cool, and you rarely hold a grudge long enough to remember why. The lesson is slower. Some feelings only show what they are if you let them sit a minute before you answer them.",
  "MOON_Cancer": "The Moon rules Cancer, so feeling is your native language. You're tuned to everyone in the room, you remember exactly how things felt years ago, and you need a home, a family or a place you belong in order to feel right. You nurture and protect without being asked. Your soft center is well guarded, sometimes too well: you can be needed by everyone and known by almost no one, and you tend to pull in just when you'd do better to reach out.",
  "MOON_Capricorn": "The old books call Capricorn a hard sign for the Moon, and it shows in how you handle your feelings: privately, efficiently, like a task. You feel safest when you're competent and don't need anyone. You're dutiful, reserved and very reliable. You probably learned early to armor up and call it strength. Being looked after now and then doesn't make you weak, and you can let people try.",
  "MOON_Gemini": "You feel by talking. A mood isn't real to you until you've named it, turned it over from three angles and told someone about it. Variety soothes you; one mood for too long feels like a locked room. You're light, curious and quick to see the funny side. Just notice when the narration gets ahead of the feeling, because you can describe an emotion beautifully and still keep it at arm's length.",
  "MOON_Leo": "Your feelings are generous, a little dramatic and meant to be witnessed. You need affection, appreciation and the warmth of being noticed, and you give all of it back twice over: loyal, big hearted, the first to celebrate someone else. The tender spot is the audience. Your warmth is real whether or not anyone is clapping, and you feel better once you believe that.",
  "MOON_Libra": "You feel safe when the people around you are at peace. A tense room gets under your skin fast, and you're gifted at smoothing it: gracious, fair, tuned to everyone's mood. Partnership and beauty settle you. Your risk is disappearing into the peacekeeping, agreeing so smoothly that you lose track of what you actually feel and want.",
  "MOON_Pisces": "You feel everything, often before anyone says a word. Your emotions are oceanic and porous, and you pick up a room's mood the second you walk in. Solitude, imagination and some sense of a bigger connection restore you. You're gentle and endlessly compassionate. With no skin between you and the world, you can lose your own feelings in everyone else's, so keep asking which of these emotions are actually yours.",
  "MOON_Sagittarius": "You need room. Freedom, space and something to aim at keep your spirits up, and fences make you itchy. You're warm, buoyant and sure things will work out, and usually they do. The habit to watch is the exit. When a feeling gets heavy you'd rather be on the road, and you're still learning that staying through a hard patch is its own kind of freedom.",
  "MOON_Scorpio": "The old books put the Moon in its fall in Scorpio, and you know the reason: you feel far more than you show. Your emotions run deep, all or nothing, and you don't hold anything lightly. You trust slowly, guard your privacy and stay loyal for life. So much unshown feeling builds pressure, and you can brood or suspect when a straight question would do. Letting someone in is the risk that actually eases it.",
  "MOON_Taurus": "The Moon is exalted in Taurus, its happiest sign in the old books, and you feel it as calm. Your emotions run steady, slow and very physical: good food, soft sheets, a routine that holds. You steady the people around you without trying. When it goes wrong, the calm turns immovable, and you can hang onto a comfort or a grudge long past its use and call it peace.",
  "MOON_Virgo": "When you're upset, you tidy something. Order, routine and being useful are how you settle your feelings, and you're happiest when you're quietly helping. You notice what needs doing before anyone asks. The trouble starts when you aim that sharp eye at your own heart and go looking for the flaw. Not every feeling is a problem to solve. Some just need to be felt and left alone.",
  "NORTH_NODE_Aquarius": "Your growth runs toward the group: shared aims, equality and an identity rooted in something bigger than your own spotlight. Your South Node in Leo holds the old pull of applause and making it about you. Serving the many can feel like giving up the stage. Belong as an equal, and spend your gifts on the whole.",
  "NORTH_NODE_Aries": "You're growing toward yourself: independence, courage and the nerve to want things and act without waiting for everyone to agree. Your South Node in Libra is the old ease, deferring and accommodating and defining yourself through other people. Pleasing comes so naturally that wanting can feel foreign. Before you ask what everyone else would prefer, ask what you want first.",
  "NORTH_NODE_Cancer": "You're learning to feel: vulnerability, care and the courage to need people instead of handling everything alone. The South Node in Capricorn is your old armor of control and self sufficiency. Softness can feel like exposure. Let your guard down enough to be looked after. Needing someone isn't weakness.",
  "NORTH_NODE_Capricorn": "Responsibility is where you're growing: maturity, self mastery and a contribution that comes from standing on your own. The South Node in Cancer is the old comfort of retreat and the familiar. Taking charge can feel like too much to carry. Become your own authority. Step out of the shell and into a real role in the world.",
  "NORTH_NODE_Gemini": "Curiosity is where you're headed: listening, asking real questions and staying open to the facts that complicate what you already believe. Your South Node in Sagittarius is the comfort of the sweeping conclusion and the feeling of already knowing. Gather the details before you reach for the meaning, and let other minds actually change yours.",
  "NORTH_NODE_Leo": "Your growth runs toward your own heart: creative courage, warmth and the nerve to be visible as one particular person instead of blending into the group. Your South Node in Aquarius is the safety of the crowd and a cool distance. Being seen can feel dangerously exposed. Dare to shine as yourself anyway.",
  "NORTH_NODE_Libra": "You're growing toward partnership: cooperation, fairness and real consideration for another person instead of charging ahead alone. Your South Node in Aries is the old ease of independence and putting yourself first. Meeting someone halfway can feel like surrender. It isn't. You can find out who you are through relationships, not only against them.",
  "NORTH_NODE_Pisces": "You're learning to let go: compassion, faith and trust in a current larger than you, instead of the endless need to fix and control. The South Node in Virgo is your old ease with criticism, managing and perfecting. Letting go can feel like losing your grip. Trade some control for compassion, and trust what you can't manage or fully understand.",
  "NORTH_NODE_Sagittarius": "You're headed toward meaning: faith, the big picture and trusting your intuition instead of gathering data forever. Your South Node in Gemini holds the old ease of cleverness and second guessing. Conviction can feel like a leap. Commit to a direction and a belief, and let understanding grow past information.",
  "NORTH_NODE_Scorpio": "Depth is your direction: transformation, shared intimacy and the courage to let things end and change instead of clinging to comfort. The South Node in Taurus is the old habit of holding on and keeping things the same. Intensity can feel like losing solid ground. Allow the change your comfort was built to prevent, and trust what grows back.",
  "NORTH_NODE_Taurus": "Your direction is steadiness: a worth built on your own ground, not borrowed from intensity or crisis. The South Node in Scorpio holds the old habit of upheaval, merging and living inside other people's dramas. Simple and solid can feel almost too quiet at first. Let your security be plain and self made. Calm is not the same as boring.",
  "NORTH_NODE_Virgo": "Order is your direction: discernment, useful work and the dignity of showing up for practical things. The South Node in Pisces is the old pull toward drift and escape. The grounded and exact can feel small after the boundless. Bring some form to the fog. Tending the daily is how you get somewhere.",
  "SATURN_Aquarius": "Uranus rules Aquarius now, but Saturn ruled it for two thousand years before, and you work through systems, principles and a serious commitment to the long future. You build structures that serve many people. Ideals held too coldly can lose the human warmth they were meant for. Keep your principles close to the people they're for.",
  "SATURN_Aries": "Aries is Saturn's fall: restraint dropped into pure impulse. For you that means confidence doesn't come free; you build it over years. Your urge to act meets an inner brake, and you can hesitate and second guess your own first moves. The boldness you lack at the start shows up through doing, not before it. Start anyway.",
  "SATURN_Cancer": "Cancer is one of Saturn's two detriments, and your feelings meet a hard structure: guarded, managed, kept behind a wall you built early. You look for security through control more than trust. Your warmth is real, just slow to show. You may have learned to armor your softness and call it strength. Letting someone in isn't the danger you were taught it was.",
  "SATURN_Capricorn": "Saturn rules Capricorn, so you're on home ground: discipline, ambition and mastery come naturally, and you build your life through patient, responsible climbing. Authority comes to you with time. You can become nothing but your achievements, a structure so load bearing it forgets it's a person. Let warmth and rest in; nothing will collapse.",
  "SATURN_Gemini": "You think seriously. Your mind is structured and slow to commit until it's sure, and your mastery comes through careful study and careful speech. There may be an early fear of not knowing enough. Don't wait for certainty before you speak; a thought worth having is worth saying before it's flawless.",
  "SATURN_Leo": "Leo is the other sign where Saturn is in detriment, and for you the urge to shine collides with a fear of being seen and found wanting. You feel you have to earn your creativity and pride, and praise is hard to trust. So you may hold back your own warmth and play to avoid exposure. Let it out before you feel fully ready. That's the only way it ripens.",
  "SATURN_Libra": "Saturn is exalted in Libra, its most constructive sign by Lilly's rules, and you bring your discipline to fairness, commitment and the serious work of keeping a bond. You're good at balance and at sharing responsibility. Duty can harden into coolness, keeping your relationships correct but distant. Let some warmth into the structure you uphold so reliably.",
  "SATURN_Pisces": "Your work is giving shape to the formless: building a vessel for intuition, faith and compassion. You master things through disciplined kindness and grounded belief. You may fear the very depths you live near, either walling them off or getting lost in them. Learn to hold the boundless without drowning in it.",
  "SATURN_Sagittarius": "You build your beliefs carefully. Faith gets tested, not assumed, and you approach freedom with a sober eye. Your convictions are earned and examined. Caution can shrink your horizon to what feels safe. Trust the larger view enough to commit to it and live by it.",
  "SATURN_Scorpio": "You discipline the depths. Control, endurance and mastery of intense feeling are your work, and your will can outlast almost anything. You guard your vulnerability fiercely. Control can become its own cage, armor against ever being exposed or betrayed. The letting go you fear most is what finally relieves the pressure.",
  "SATURN_Taurus": "You build to last. You're disciplined through patience and the slow making of real security, and you won't be hurried. You need solid ground under you. That need can turn into a fear of losing what you have, gripping it and refusing every risk. Some things have to be ventured before they can be kept.",
  "SATURN_Virgo": "You build through precision: method, exactness and the patient perfecting of a craft. You're diligent and quietly demanding, mostly of yourself. That standard can turn into relentless self criticism, as if flawless were the price of worth. Your competence is real long before the work is perfect.",
  "SUN_Aquarius": "You run on your own frequency: independence, ideas and a future you can already half see. You care about principles and the big picture, and you come across original, engaged and friendly at a slight distance. The old books call Aquarius a hard sign for the Sun, and you'll know why: you can watch your own life from one step back, so devoted to the cause that the warm, particular you gets held at arm's length.",
  "SUN_Aries": "Your Sun is exalted in Aries, its best sign in the old books, and you run on starting things. You come alive when there's something to begin, a challenge to meet head on, a front to lead from. People notice you without your trying, mostly because you're already moving. Your weak spot is the middle of things. You love the first day of a project so much that the four hundredth can feel like someone else's problem. Your best work happens when you stay past the thrill.",
  "SUN_Cancer": "You build your life around care, memory and the people and places that count as home. Your energy rises and falls with your feelings, and you draw strength from belonging and give it back as warmth. You seem gentle, and you're far more protective than you look. Then there's the shell. You guard your soft center so well that being needed can stand in for being known, and you pull inward right when you need people most.",
  "SUN_Capricorn": "You build yourself on responsibility and on something real taking shape over years. Discipline suits you, and so does standing you've actually earned. You carry authority without asking for it, and people lean on you. Just don't turn into the structure. You're allowed to be a person too, warm and unfinished, and not only the thing everyone else holds onto.",
  "SUN_Gemini": "You're a moving target, and you like it that way. You come alive in conversation, in questions, in the next interesting idea, and your mind keeps drawing lines between things nobody else thought were connected. People find you bright and easy to like. Watch for scatter: a dozen half finished interests, each brilliant for a week, and a real you that's hard to locate under all the versions you try on.",
  "SUN_Leo": "The Sun rules Leo, so you're at home here, and you're meant to shine out loud. You run on creativity, play and warm attention, given and returned, and you carry a natural pride that usually earns the looks it gets. The question worth asking now and then: is the warmth shining because that's who you are, or because the room is watching? The first kind never runs out.",
  "SUN_Libra": "You come into focus between people: in fairness, in balance, in meeting someone halfway. You're happiest making harmony and beauty, and people find you poised and easy to be around. The old books put the Sun at its weakest in Libra, and the trouble is the one you'd guess: you can sand your edges down so smoothly that you lose track of what you want when nobody else is in the room.",
  "SUN_Pisces": "Your sense of self is porous: intuitive, imaginative, tuned to something bigger than you. You're fed by compassion and a faith that doesn't need proof, and you're hard to pin down because you shift to match whoever's near you. What you lack is an edge. You can soak up so much of a room that you lose your own outline, and you have to keep finding yourself behind all that lovely openness.",
  "SUN_Sagittarius": "You build yourself around meaning, freedom and a horizon that's always a little further on. You light up for learning, travel and the sense that life is bigger than this room, and people find you frank, warm and contagiously hopeful. Restlessness is the cost. You can mistake the next horizon for arriving, and leave before anyone gets the chance to really know you.",
  "SUN_Scorpio": "You build yourself around depth: privacy, intensity and the nerve to look at what other people look away from. You run on emotional truth and you're capable of real reinvention, ending an old version of yourself and coming back changed. You hold a lot back, and people find that magnetic. Control is the risk. The armor can work so well that it keeps out the closeness you want most.",
  "SUN_Taurus": "You build a self slowly and make it last. You steady a room just by not rushing, and you feel most like yourself around what's solid, sensory and actually yours: a good meal, a well made thing, a place you've paid for. Your patience outlasts flashier people. Left alone, that steadiness turns into refusing to move, and you can dig in long after the ground has shifted.",
  "SUN_Virgo": "You find yourself in craft: doing a thing well, noticing what's off, making it better. Your energy comes from good work and a body you look after, and you tend to undersell how capable you actually are. Your inner critic aims at you first. You're allowed to exist before you've been useful, and you're whole before you've been fixed.",
  "VENUS_Aquarius": "You love at a friendly distance. Shared ideas, independence and a connection that doesn't demand too much closeness appeal to you, and you're drawn to the unusual. You're loyal but cool. Prizing freedom this highly can mean never letting anyone all the way in, so let a relationship ask something of you now and then.",
  "VENUS_Aries": "Love, for you, is a chase: fast, direct and thrilling. You're attracted to nerve and heat, and your affection is honest and generous in the moment. Lilly counts Aries against Venus, because the planet of ease is sitting in the sign of the fight. You'll recognize it if you've ever lost interest the second someone said yes. The deeper pleasure starts after the chase is over, and it's worth staying for.",
  "VENUS_Cancer": "You love tenderly. For you, attraction is tied up with safety and care, with the wish to nurture and be nurtured, and home is the truest romance there is. You're protective, sentimental and you remember exactly how love felt. When you're scared, you hold on tighter, and that can smother the closeness you want. Real care leaves room to breathe.",
  "VENUS_Capricorn": "You love seriously. Attraction is slow to kindle and built to last, and you're drawn to substance, reliability and someone who's going somewhere. You show affection by showing up, not with flourishes. Your heart can stay too guarded, treating the relationship like a contract and holding back warmth until trust is fully proven. Let some tenderness show before all the evidence is in.",
  "VENUS_Gemini": "You fall for a mind. Wit, conversation and the spark of a quick exchange do it for you, and you're charmed by anyone genuinely interesting to talk to. You're playful, curious and light, and variety keeps your feelings alive. The risk is staying at the clever surface, sampling connections. Let one of them go deep enough to become more than a great conversation.",
  "VENUS_Leo": "You love grandly. You're drawn to romance done boldly and loyalty worn out loud, and you'd rather celebrate love than keep it quiet. Your affection is theatrical and wholehearted. On insecure days you can need constant admiration to feel safe in a relationship. Trust that the warmth is real even when nobody's performing it back to you.",
  "VENUS_Libra": "Venus rules Libra, so love is your native art: harmony, fairness and the real pleasure of meeting someone halfway. You're drawn to grace, balance and beauty, and your affection is considerate and easy to receive. You can get so set on keeping the peace that your own wants disappear. Stay a distinct person inside the harmony you work so hard to keep.",
  "VENUS_Pisces": "Pisces is where Venus is exalted, and you love at full tenderness: boundless, compassionate, deeply romantic. You're drawn to the soulful and the wounded, and you give without keeping score. Your blind spot is falling for the dream of someone and missing who they actually are. Love the real one, with your eyes open.",
  "VENUS_Sagittarius": "You love freely. Adventure, honesty and the promise of shared horizons attract you, and so does anyone who makes the world feel bigger. Your affection is warm and frank, and you hate being fenced in. Your pattern is loving the open road more than the person on it, and bolting when a bond asks for real commitment. Staying can be an adventure too.",
  "VENUS_Scorpio": "Venus is in detriment in Scorpio by the old rules, and your heart doesn't do casual. Your love runs deep, intense, all or nothing. You're drawn to what's hidden and hard to reach, and you're fiercely loyal and fiercely private. So much feeling can turn into jealousy or a fear of betrayal. Trust enough to let the bond breathe instead of guarding it.",
  "VENUS_Taurus": "Venus rules Taurus, so you love the way the planet likes best: through the senses, loyally, built to last. Touch, comfort, good food and steady devotion are your love language, and you take pleasure slowly and without apology. You're warm and dependable. Hold things loosely enough, though, because a person or a comfort gripped like property stops being freely given.",
  "VENUS_Virgo": "Venus has its fall in Virgo, and you show love the Virgo way: through service, attention and the small acts of care that say more than any speech. You're modest, useful, a little reserved, and your standards are high. The critic in your heart can pick at a partner's flaws, or hold you back until you feel worthy. Love was never meant to be earned through perfection, yours or theirs."
}

export const YOU_IN_HOUSE: Record<string, string> = {
  "CHIRON_H1": "In the myth, Chiron was the wise centaur, a healer and teacher of heroes, who was struck by a poisoned arrow and couldn't cure himself. Astrologers borrowed the story whole. In your 1st house, the sore spot sits right where everyone can see it.\n\nThat might be something visible, or a body that didn't match what other kids had. Or it's subtler: a feeling of being too much or not enough that colors every first meeting. You may have spent your early years hyperaware of how you came across, rehearsing entrances and apologizing for taking up room. What comes out of it is an unusual gentleness toward anyone new, awkward or out of place. You notice whoever's standing alone at the edge of the party. Usually you go over and stand there too.",
  "CHIRON_H10": "Chiron was spotted in 1977, an odd small body circling between Saturn and Uranus, and astrologers took it up quickly. In your 10th house of career and reputation, it often shows up as a sore spot about being seen succeeding.\n\nImpostor feelings are common, and praise doesn't quite land. Your parents may have expected too much, or nothing, or struggled publicly in a way that left a mark. Your career may bend sharply, through a failure, an embarrassment or a calling that arrived late. Your work may come to help others with exactly what once tripped you up: the former dropout who becomes a principal, the burned out executive who starts coaching. The diploma on the wall is real. You still glance at it sometimes, as if to check.",
  "CHIRON_H11": "Always a little outside the circle: that's the feeling under your Chiron, even when you're well liked.\n\nIn the house of friends and groups, yours may go back to being left out: the playground clique, the team that didn't pick you, a friend group that turned on you in eighth grade. Grown up, you can join groups and still feel like a visitor, and hoping again can feel risky after early disappointments. Out of that comes a gift for including people. You notice who's on the edge and who left the party early without saying goodbye. You start the club for misfits or the online group for people with the same rare problem. Your friendships are few and deep, and you remember to invite the new person.",
  "CHIRON_H12": "Chiron is hard to classify: found as a minor planet, then caught showing a faint comet's haze, it now sits on both lists. In the 12th, the house of hidden things, it keeps that quality. The hurt is hard to name.\n\nThere may be something you can't put words to: an inherited grief, a vague sense of guilt, a family sorrow from before you were born. It can show up as anxiety, as loneliness in a crowd or as a sense of soaking up everyone else's pain. Your quiet gift is compassion for anyone struggling out of sight, and serving in the places the world doesn't look may pull at you. Meditation, prayer, art and long solitary walks help you. Few people ever find out how much you carry, and most of the people you help never learn your name.",
  "CHIRON_H2": "Some people never feel they've earned their keep, no matter what the paycheck says. With Chiron in the 2nd, that feeling can follow you through every raise.\n\nMaybe there was scarcity early, or a family where worth was tied to usefulness, or a moment of money shame that never quite faded. It can linger whatever you earn: underpricing your work, saving against a disaster that never comes, giving things away because keeping them feels undeserved. A friend's new house can sting for a week. The flip side is real wisdom about value. You know better than most what money can and can't fix, and you may become the friend people call before a big purchase, or the counselor who never judges, because you remember exactly what the overdraft notice felt like.",
  "CHIRON_H3": "The kid who stumbled through every oral report sometimes grows up to give the best toast at the wedding. That's one version of a 3rd house Chiron, in the house of speech, learning and siblings.\n\nEarly learning may have come with a snag: a learning difference, a teacher who said you weren't smart, a family where the wrong words got punished, a sibling relationship that hurt. Speaking up can feel risky as a result. You might prepare notes for phone calls, or go quiet for years and then, one day, not. A mind that worked hard to be understood tends to understand others. You could be a gifted teacher, tutor, translator or writer, especially for people who struggle, because you remember being on the other side of the desk.",
  "CHIRON_H4": "Home was the sore spot. With Chiron here, the hurt sits at the root: family, childhood, the place you were supposed to feel safe.\n\nYour early home might have been unstable, cold, chaotic or just not quite a fit, as if you were the kid who felt adopted even though you weren't. One of your parents may have been hurting too, and passed along what they couldn't heal. Belonging can feel both precious and unreliable to you. So you build home for others: the friend with the couch everyone's slept on, the safe house for three generations. Your own sense of home may arrive late and on purpose: a house bought at fifty, a front porch, a door that's never locked during the day.",
  "CHIRON_H5": "What happens to a kid who was told to stop showing off? You may know. The 5th covers play, creativity, romance and children, and your tender spot is the simple right to enjoy something and be seen enjoying it.\n\nYour creative confidence can be fragile. You may have real talent and hide it, making art in private and never showing it. Romance can carry an old fear of not being chosen, and children can be a tender subject in their own ways. And yet you're often wonderful with kids, especially shy ones, and the art you finally share is the honest kind. A late first gallery show, a children's book written at sixty, a band joined after retirement: that's the shape it often takes.",
  "CHIRON_H6": "In the myth, Chiron taught medicine to Asclepius, who became the Greek god of healing: a fitting backstory for Chiron in the house of daily work and care.\n\nWork may be where it hurt: jobs that went badly, a sense of never being useful enough, or wearing yourself out trying to prove you were. Your own body and routine may have asked a lot of patience from you. Out of that comes a knack for care. Health work, therapy, rehab or caregiving may call you, and you're skilled at it because you listen like someone who's needed help. You know what it's like to be the one who needs help, and you never make anyone feel small for asking.",
  "CHIRON_H7": "The friend who gives the best relationship advice has often had the hardest relationships. A 7th house Chiron is one way that story starts.\n\nMaybe there was an early betrayal, a painful split in the family, a pattern of choosing partners who needed rescuing, or a deep fear of being left. Relationships can feel like the place you're most exposed. You might avoid commitment for years, or commit fast and then wait for the floor to give way. What you end up with is an unusual understanding of how people fit together and how they come apart. You may become a counselor, a mediator or simply the one everyone calls after a breakup. Your own good partnership, when you find it, is honest in a way that took effort to learn.",
  "CHIRON_H8": "You've probably been through something you don't talk about at dinner. Your Chiron sits in the territory of loss, intimacy, trust and debt, the parts of life most people would rather skip.\n\nAn early betrayal, a family crisis or a money disaster may have changed how safe the world felt, and intimacy can be complicated afterward. Trust arrives in small amounts, and closeness can feel like handing someone a knife. And yet you're an extraordinary person to have nearby when things go wrong. You sit with grief without flinching, and crisis work or counseling may draw you, along with anyone who needs a steady voice in a terrible hour. You know the territory and don't pretend it's anything other than what it is, and people trust you for exactly that.",
  "CHIRON_H9": "Chiron the centaur taught heroes, Achilles and Jason among them, which makes your 9th house of teaching, belief and long journeys a natural home for it.\n\nWhat aches is meaning. A faith that broke, an upbringing that used belief as a stick, an education that got interrupted, a sense of being shut out from the big questions because nobody thought you were smart enough. You may distrust every teacher and system for years, or keep searching, one belief after another, hoping the next one fits. Your teaching gift, when it arrives, is a humble one. You're good with students who've been failed before, you can explain a hard idea without making anyone feel stupid, and you're comfortable saying you don't know.",
  "JUPITER_H1": "The big laugh at the back of the restaurant is often yours. Jupiter in the 1st house makes you larger than life, sometimes in spirit, sometimes in build, often both.\n\nJupiter was the great benefic in the old texts, the planet of growth, generosity and good luck, and in the 1st it sits right on you. You come across warm, optimistic and a little expansive, and people trust you fast. Doors open. A job turns up through someone you met in line at the bank, and you talk about it later as if that's just how jobs happen. For you, often, it is. Excess is the snag: promises outrun the calendar, portions outrun the appetite, and confidence runs a few steps ahead of the facts. None of it dents your good mood for long, which is either the best thing about you or the most maddening, depending on who you ask.",
  "JUPITER_H10": "Some careers have a tailwind, and Jupiter in the 10th tends to supply one, often visible from outside long before you feel it.\n\nPromotions come, and so do public roles, a reputation for fairness and good humor and a name people trust. You're drawn to work bigger than a paycheck: law, teaching, politics, religion, publishing, running something with a mission. Mentors appear at the right moment, often a parent or early boss who believed in you out loud, and later you're remembered as the generous boss who wrote recommendation letters without being asked twice. Overreach is the risk: taking the bigger job before the smaller one is done, promising more than the year can deliver, coasting on a reputation. Public success can also make private doubt hard to admit. Admit it anyway, to someone.",
  "JUPITER_H11": "Good Spirit was the oldest name for the 11th house, and Jupiter was happiest there. Friends, allies, patrons, hopes: the house of the people who help, given to the planet of help.\n\nIt's one of Jupiter's most comfortable spots. You have friends in many places, including surprisingly useful ones: the college roommate who became a judge, the neighbor who knows someone at the hospital. Groups welcome you. You join causes, clubs, boards and congregations, and you keep the group hopeful when the numbers look bad. Your hopes are big, and more often than seems fair, they come true. Joining too much is the risk: six boards, four committees and a generosity the less scrupulous members figure out fast. Your address book is still the envy of everyone you know.",
  "JUPITER_H12": "Things work out at the last minute for you. Not always, but often enough that you may feel looked after by something you can't name.\n\nThe 12th is the hidden house: solitude, retreat, the unconscious and the things that happen out of sight. Before Neptune was found, Jupiter ruled Pisces, the 12th sign, and traditional astrologers still use that rulership, which puts faith itself in the house of the unseen. It brings a quiet, private generosity: anonymous donations, volunteering nobody posts about, a spiritual life you mostly keep to yourself. Faith can slide into avoidance, the problem left for the universe to handle. At your best, you're the stranger who stays in the waiting room at three in the morning.",
  "JUPITER_H2": "Money tends to show up for you. Not always a lot, and not always on time, but you land on your feet financially in a way your friends find slightly unfair.\n\nThe 2nd is the house of income, possessions and values, and Jupiter is the planet of more. Teaching, publishing, law, travel, sales or anything that grows by word of mouth can pay you well. You're generous with what you have: quick to pick up the check, quick to lend, slow to ask for it back. You believe there's enough to go around, and you act like it. The weak spot is assuming more is coming. Spending rises to meet income and then politely passes it, and your credit card has heard every reason. You'll usually be fine. That's the frustrating part.",
  "JUPITER_H3": "You can turn a trip to the post office into a twenty minute story with a moral at the end.\n\nThe 3rd covers daily talk, siblings, neighbors, school, writing and short trips, and Jupiter enlarges all of it. You're a generous talker and an eager learner, reading three books at once and quoting all of them. A sibling may be a real source of luck: the one who found you a first job, or who's still your best friend. Neighbors know your name, and teaching, writing, broadcasting and sales come naturally, because explaining things is a pleasure. Gemini, the 3rd sign, is hard on Jupiter, and you'll see a hint of it in a big mind spread thin across a small territory, with lots of opinions, not all of them checked. Your stories improve every time you tell them, and nobody at the table minds.",
  "JUPITER_H4": "Your house is probably bigger than it needs to be: an extra bedroom, a long table, a fridge stocked for guests who haven't been invited yet. Jupiter in the 4th wants home to be generous.\n\nCancer is the 4th sign and the sign of Jupiter's exaltation, so this is one of the places the great benefic is easiest to see at work. Your family is likely large or loud or warm, or all three, and a parent, grandparent or hometown may have given you a sense that the world is basically safe. You may own property, sometimes more than one place, and the family home can stay in the picture for decades. Your nest can get a little too comfortable, though. Leaving can take longer than it should, and taking everyone in can fill the house with people who never quite leave either. Thanksgiving at your place runs to three tables.",
  "JUPITER_H5": "You may have the most godchildren in the family. Jupiter in the 5th is generous toward anything young, playful or newly made.\n\nThe 5th covers children, romance, pleasure, creativity and risk taken for fun, and your Jupiter turns the volume up. Your love affairs tend to be big and memorable: a first date in a hot air balloon, a little much and completely sincere. Your creative work sprawls: the novel that grew to nine hundred pages, the garden that took over the side yard. Children are a real source of pride, yours or other people's, and you're the adult every kid wants at the party. Luck at games is a common modern reading, and you may have it. Or you may only think you do. That usually becomes clear around the third trip to Reno.",
  "JUPITER_H6": "There's always one more project on your desk. Jupiter in the 6th says yes to work, then says yes again.\n\nThe 6th covers jobs, daily routine and service, and your Jupiter brings growth, sometimes the good kind and sometimes the overloaded kind. Work comes easily and keeps coming. Coworkers like you and bosses lean on you, and you may find work where helping people is the actual job: medicine, social work, teaching, counseling. Offers come because someone remembered how cheerful you were on a bad Tuesday. The excess shows in the schedule: a routine that keeps expanding, rich food at every office party, a calendar with no white space left. Guard a little of your week from your own generosity.",
  "JUPITER_H7": "Partners tend to arrive bearing gifts: money, connections, a sense of humor, a family that takes you in. A 7th house Jupiter is often read as marrying well.\n\nThe 7th covers marriage, partnership, contracts and open opponents, and Jupiter makes all of them kinder. Business partners are generous, disputes tend to settle, and your enemies are rare or at least reasonable. You believe in partnership the way some people believe in church. You expect the best of whoever's across the table, and you often get it. The trouble is expecting too much: a partner cast as the answer to everything, or a yard next door that keeps looking greener. You don't love lightly. You just keep believing the next chapter will be even better, and sometimes, annoyingly, it is.",
  "JUPITER_H8": "Other people's money has a way of finding you: an inheritance, a partner's income, a settlement, an investment someone else set up years ago.\n\nThe 8th is the house of shared resources, debt, intimacy and the hard changes that remake a life, and Jupiter does surprisingly well here. Help arrives through other people, and you meet a crisis with a calm faith that things will turn out. Finance, insurance, estate law, psychology: anywhere big change and big money meet can suit you. Intimacy runs generous and deep. Debt is the flip side, because a planet that expands things expands what's owed as easily as what's owned. You're usually the calmest person in the room when the paperwork gets serious.",
  "JUPITER_H9": "Sagittarius is the 9th sign and Jupiter rules it, so your Jupiter is home, in the house of long journeys, religion, philosophy, law and higher learning, and it behaves like a planet with nothing to prove.\n\nYou collect passport stamps, degrees and opinions about the meaning of life, roughly in that order. Faith matters to you, whether it's a religion, a philosophy or a stubborn belief that people are mostly decent. Teaching, publishing, law, academia and anything that crosses cultures suit you. Foreigners and mentors tend to be lucky for you, and you'll mentor someone in turn. Your flaw is the sermon: a mind this sure of the big picture can start preaching it over dinner. You also book the next trip before unpacking from the last. Your suitcase never quite goes back in the closet.",
  "MARS_H1": "There's probably a scar with a story: a chin split open on a bike ramp at nine, a knuckle that healed crooked, a knee that still predicts rain. Your Mars lives in your body first, and your body keeps the receipts.\n\nAries is the 1st sign and Mars rules Aries, so the planet of drive stands at your front door. Your walk is quick, your handshake means it, and your opinions arrive before anyone asked. Your temper, when it flares, usually burns out within the hour. You start things: the project, the business, the argument, and you'd rather apologize later than wait for permission now. Speed is what gets you in trouble. You drive your body like a rental car and pick fights because standing still felt worse. People have told you to calm down since kindergarten. You mostly didn't.",
  "MARS_H10": "Ambition with its sleeves rolled up: Mars at the top of your chart rarely hides what it wants.\n\nCapricorn, the 10th sign, is where Mars is exalted, and your 10th house carries some of that flavor: a planet that works best with a mountain in front of it. You go after your career directly, and you thrive where toughness gets rewarded: business, construction, surgery, the military, sports, politics, anything with a clear ladder. You and authority usually clash, right up until you become the authority. Your reputation can take public hits: a burned bridge, a feud people heard about, a name for being hard to work for. Fear gets results fast and respect gets them for longer. The careers that last here belong to people who learn the difference early.",
  "MARS_H11": "Every group chat has one member who eventually types, \"Ok, are we actually doing this or not?\" With Mars in the 11th, it's usually you.\n\nFriends, causes and shared goals are 11th house business, and your Mars brings motion to them. You're an organizer, a team captain, the volunteer who ends up running the campaign. Your friendships often form around a shared mission: the team, the band, the union local, the cause. You push friends harder than they asked to be pushed, and you turn hopes into plans with deadlines. That drive has a price in groups: power struggles at the club, a falling out with a cofounder, the friend who drifted off after one argument too many. And still, when the basement floods or the fundraiser is three days out, yours is the first number anyone calls.",
  "MARS_H12": "Traditional astrology gave the 12th house secret enemies, along with exile and losses from out of sight. Put Mars, the planet of open conflict, in the house of hidden things, and your anger tends to go underground with it.\n\nYou may find direct confrontation strangely hard. Irritation gets swallowed, then comes back as sarcasm, a headache, a sleepless night or a sudden blowup over a dish left in the sink. You can turn the energy inward and become your own toughest opponent, or put it to work behind closed doors: hospitals, labs, shelters, night shifts, places that need stamina and give little credit. There's real courage here, just quiet, and you're steadier in a crisis than anyone expected. What helps most is a physical outlet, like a run, a heavy bag or a garden that needs digging, and saying the angry sentence out loud while it's still small.",
  "MARS_H2": "How much is enough? You rarely stop to ask, because earning feels like a fight and the fight feels good.\n\nThe 2nd is the house of money, possessions and values, and your Mars brings appetite to it. You probably worked early: the paper route, the summer on a roofing crew, the first car bought with cash you counted twice. Your income tends to come from effort people can see: physical work, sales, trades, commission, anything where pushing harder pays more. You defend your values out loud, sometimes at a volume the dinner party didn't need. Spending runs hot too: the impulse buy, the hunch bet, the argument over a bill that cost more than the bill. Your best money years start when you aim the drive at building, not winning.",
  "MARS_H3": "You drive like you're late. Usually you are, because you said yes to three errands on the way.\n\nYour Mars heats up the near world: siblings, neighbors, school, short trips and the constant traffic of daily talk. Your mind is quick and your mouth is quicker. You debate for sport, won't let a bad point slide in a meeting and send the reply before the other person has finished typing. Your first rival may have been a sibling, and the old competition can still flare at Thanksgiving. Your writing is punchy; teaching, reporting, sales and advocacy suit you. The cost is collateral: a sharp sentence wins the argument and loses the neighbor, and the family group text goes very quiet for a week.",
  "MARS_H4": "Somebody in your house had a temper. Not always, but often enough that you remember the sound of doors.\n\nThe 4th is home, family and roots, and Cancer, the 4th sign, is where Mars falls. Houses don't strictly inherit dignity from signs, but the image fits: a fighting planet set down in the nursery. It can mean a loud household, a parent who ran hot, or a family that did everything at full volume. As an adult you probably throw energy at the home itself. You tear out walls, rebuild the deck, move more than you planned, and do the renovation yourself because the contractor was too slow. You defend family fiercely. Anger swallowed at work tends to come out at your kitchen table, so your long project is a home that can hold some heat without burning.",
  "MARS_H5": "Pickup basketball, Sunday morning, and one player is going at it like it's game seven. That's probably you.\n\nFun, flirting, kids and creative risk all live in the 5th, and your Mars turns all of it into a contest worth winning. Romance runs fast and physical, with a real taste for the chase. Your creative work is bold, loud and willing to fail in public. With kids you're the one wrestling on the carpet, coaching the team and getting a little too invested in the science fair. Risk is part of the fun: a motorcycle, a poker table, a startup. Trouble starts when play stops being play: the board game that ends with someone leaving the table, the romance that loses interest once it's won. You'll stay competitive, but in time a good loss can make you laugh.",
  "MARS_H6": "Of all the places to give the war planet its joy, the oldest astrologers picked the house of chores. The 6th was labor, illness and toil, and Mars was the planet of cutting, burning and hard effort. One way to read it: put the worker in the workshop and it stops wrecking the rest of the house.\n\nYou attack a task instead of starting it, you hate idle afternoons, and demanding work suits you: trades, surgery, emergency services, kitchens, the military, coaching. Exercise isn't optional for you. Without it, your energy turns into irritability, bad sleep or a fight with a coworker who works at half your pace. Your body sends the bill eventually: the strain, the burn, the back that went out lifting something you should have asked for help with.",
  "MARS_H7": "You argue hardest with the people you love most, and you'd call that respect. Your Mars sits in the house of partnership.\n\nThe 7th covers marriage, close partners, contracts and the open opponent. Libra is the 7th sign, and Mars is out of place there, a fighter in the sign of manners; the house only borrows the image, but it fits. You tend to pick strong partners, sometimes combative ones, and your relationships stay lively because the friction never quite goes away. You'd make a good litigator, negotiator, agent or advocate, since fighting on someone else's behalf comes naturally. Then there's projection. If you never raise your voice, you can keep choosing partners who do. Owning your anger instead of outsourcing it is usually the turning point, and after that, the fights get fought side by side.",
  "MARS_H8": "Before Pluto was found, Mars ruled Scorpio, the 8th sign, and traditional astrologers still use that rulership. So your Mars is, by the older count, a planet working in its own basement.\n\nThe 8th holds intimacy, sex, debt, inheritance, other people's money and crisis. Your drive goes underground here. You can seem calm on the surface and run very hot underneath, and you come alive in an emergency: the nurse who gets quieter as things get worse, the investor buying while everyone sells, the one handling the arrangements while the family falls apart. Fights over shared money may show up more than you'd like. Grudges can run for decades. The hard part is power in intimacy, who needs whom and who controls what. Your trust comes slowly, and once given, it's total.",
  "MARS_H9": "What's worth fighting for? For you, the answer is usually an idea.\n\nThe 9th is belief, philosophy, religion, law, higher learning and long journeys, and your Mars makes a crusader. Your convictions come out loud and get defended with real heat, whether the subject is theology, politics or the correct way to smoke a brisket. You travel the hard way: the trek, the overland route, the country the guidebook warned about. You learn better by doing than by sitting in a lecture hall, and you might turn the fight into law, activism or coaching. At worst, your certainty meets a cousin's certainty at a holiday table. At best, you go and actually do what everyone else only believes in. Humility usually arrives late, and it makes the conviction much easier to live with.",
  "MERCURY_H1": "In the first centuries of astrology the 1st house was called the Helm, the steering oar of the chart, and said Mercury was happiest there. The planet of the mind at the helm: it fits.\n\nPeople read you as quick before you've said a word. Your eyes move; your face works things out in public. You may look and sound younger than your age, and you were probably labeled the smart one early, which came with its own pressure. Thinking and talking are part of who you are, not tools you pick up, so silence can feel strangely like disappearing. Nervous energy shows in your hands, the foot tapping under the table, the sentence you abandon halfway. Ask you a simple question and the answer arrives before the question is done, sometimes to a different question.",
  "MERCURY_H10": "The work you're known for is your thinking. Mercury in the 10th, the house of career and reputation, puts your mind on public display.\n\nYour career likely runs on communication: media, teaching, writing, sales, public speaking, law, anything with information at the center. You may change careers more than once or run several at once, and you can explain what you do to a stranger at a wedding. Your reputation rides on the quality of your ideas and how you phrase them, and a mentor who taught you to write, speak or sell may turn out to be the turning point of your whole working life. Watch for a mind that never clocks out, where every idea is a pitch and every party is networking. What steadies you is one thread your varied work keeps coming back to, so your name ends up meaning something specific.",
  "MERCURY_H11": "Everyone has a friend who says, \"Oh, you have to meet my friend.\" Often that friend is you.\n\nThe 11th covers friends, networks, groups and hopes, and your Mercury puts your mind in the middle of the crowd. You're a connector. You know a lot of people, remember who does what and love introducing the right two at the right moment. Your friendships often start with a conversation that never really stopped, and you probably live in group chats, clubs and a long running argument with the same people every holiday. Ideas about the future pull you in: technology, social change, plans a group makes together. Watch for testing ideas by whether the circle will like them. Your phone has more contacts than anyone you know, and you actually remember most of them.",
  "MERCURY_H12": "Mercury never strays far from the Sun, about 28 degrees at most, so a 12th house Mercury often means a birth around sunrise. Your mind was up early, and it learned to work quietly.\n\nYou have a large private mind. Thoughts arrive as hunches, images and half dreams, a sense of knowing that's hard to explain. Writing alone probably comes easier than talking in a group, and you do your best thinking late at night, in the shower or on long drives, when nobody's awake to interrupt. You keep secrets well, yours and other people's. The risk is a voice that never quite comes out: ideas stay locked up because saying them feels risky, and worry loops in the dark with nobody to check it against. The best idea in the meeting is often the one you mentioned afterward, quietly, in the hallway.",
  "MERCURY_H2": "Mercury was the god of merchants, and also of thieves, which says something about how the ancient world saw commerce. In your 2nd house of money and possessions, that old job description comes right back.\n\nYour mind turns toward value: what's this worth, what will it be worth, who's overpaying. You're likely a good negotiator, good with numbers and quick to spot the angle nobody priced in. You may earn through words or information: sales, writing, teaching, trading, consulting. Several income streams are common, including a side hustle that started as a joke. Just don't judge every idea by whether it pays. Some of your best ones won't. And the account doesn't need checking quite that often.",
  "MERCURY_H3": "Who calls three people during a ten minute drive? Very often, you.\n\nThis is Mercury's natural house: Gemini is the 3rd sign and Mercury rules Gemini, so the planet of communication lands in the house of communication. Siblings, neighbors, short trips, school and the steady traffic of an ordinary day are your territory. You know the shortcuts, which store has the better produce, and what the guy at the hardware store said about the new zoning. A brother or sister was probably your first debate partner. Range is never your problem; depth sometimes is. The moments that change your life tend to be the ones where you pick one thing and stay with it well past the point of novelty.",
  "MERCURY_H4": "At the family funeral, you know which cousin married whom and why two uncles stopped speaking in 1987. Your Mercury lives at home, and home is where your mind does its best and strangest work.\n\nFamily talk shaped how you think, either because your household discussed everything or because the important things went unsaid and you had to piece them together. Your memory for the past is strong. You may work from home, or keep a house full of books, papers and projects spread over the dining table, and you might become the keeper of the family records and the recipes in your grandmother's handwriting. Your long task is sorting which opinions you inherited from which ones you chose. A mind rooted this deep can carry a parent's arguments for decades without noticing.",
  "MERCURY_H5": "Puns. Board games that run past midnight. A love letter that's mostly jokes.\n\nYour Mercury makes your mind playful. Ideas are toys first and tools second, and the house of romance, children and creativity gives them plenty of room. You flirt through conversation, and your quick mind is often the most attractive thing about you. Your creative work tends to run on language: writing, comedy, songwriting, teaching kids, anything where cleverness gets to show off. You're great with children, partly because you still think a little like one. Watch for cleverness for its own sake, where the joke lands and the point drowns. The best line at the funeral usually comes from you, and somehow it's the one that makes everyone cry.",
  "MERCURY_H6": "Virgo is the 6th sign and Mercury rules Virgo, so this is one of Mercury's natural homes: work, routine, health and the craft of doing a job right. Your analytical mind ends up in charge of the details.\n\nYou actually read the manual. You know how the system works, where it breaks and what the checklist is missing. Your work likely involves information, analysis, editing or troubleshooting, and you're good at it in a way nobody notices until you're on vacation and everything falls apart. Your nerves and health run close together: worry lands in your stomach, your sleep, your jaw. Your mind doesn't clock out when the shift ends. Point that analytical eye at rest itself, and treat downtime as part of the system, not a bug in it.",
  "MERCURY_H7": "Contracts. The 7th house covers partnership, marriage, agreements and open disputes, and your Mercury puts the conversation at the center of every relationship. Not coldly. You just want to know what was agreed.\n\nA good marriage, for you, is a long conversation, and a good business partner is someone who argues back. You're a natural negotiator, mediator and translator between people who can't hear each other, and you think best in dialogue: you find out what you believe by saying it to someone across the table. The flip side is that decisions can stall until someone else weighs in, and your view can drift toward whoever spoke last. Your mind can work alone just fine. Your best partnerships are the ones where both of you keep your own voice.",
  "MERCURY_H8": "You read the last page first. Then the footnotes. Then the thing the author was clearly avoiding.\n\nYour Mercury sends your mind into the territory of secrets, debt, inheritance, sex, death and other people's money. You're a natural investigator. Small talk feels almost painful; you want the real story and the motive under the motive. Research, psychology, forensic work, tax law and insurance come easily, and people tell you things they've never told anyone. A mind trained to look underneath can find hidden motives everywhere, though, including in people who have none, and a fear or grudge can loop for years. At your best, you can sit with a hard truth and say it plainly and kindly to someone who needs to hear it.",
  "MERCURY_H9": "The 9th is Sagittarius's natural house, and Sagittarius is where Mercury is weakest. A house doesn't carry dignity the way a sign does, but the tension echoes: the planet of facts and details lands in the house of big pictures and big beliefs.\n\nIt often makes you a lifelong student. You read widely, argue philosophy at parties, pick up languages and want to know how the whole thing fits together. Travel feeds your mind directly, and you may end up teaching, writing, publishing, practicing law or translating between cultures. The tension shows up as missing details: a mind tuned to the grand theory can skip the small fact that would have changed the conclusion. Somewhere in your house is a shelf of books in a language you meant to finish learning.",
  "MOON_H1": "Ancient astrologers gave the Moon the body. Put it in the 1st house, the house of the body and the face, and the two land on top of each other: whatever's happening inside you shows on the outside, usually before you've decided to share it.\n\nSo you're readable. Your mood is in your eyes, your shoulders, the way you come through a door. Strangers tell you things on buses and babies stare at you. You respond to whoever's in front of you, which makes you warm company and leaves you a little at the mercy of the room. A tense meeting follows you home; a good dinner lifts you for days. Your friends can tell how your week went before you've taken your coat off.",
  "MOON_H10": "In the branch of astrology that reads charts for nations, the Moon stands for the people: the crowd, the public mood. In your chart it sits at the top, in the 10th house of career and reputation, and your working life tends to involve exactly that.\n\nYou're drawn to work with the public in it: hospitality, food, nursing, real estate, teaching, any job with a following that feels personal. You become known for how you make people feel. Your mother's hopes, spoken or not, may have shaped your ambition. Your reputation waxes and wanes like the Moon, and you feel each phase. A good review lifts your week; a bad one sinks it. You've read the comments section, and you wish you hadn't.",
  "MOON_H11": "You're the friend who remembers the dog had surgery last week and texts to ask how it went, and the one who organizes the reunion. Your heart lives in friendship.\n\nThe 11th house covers friends, groups and hopes, and your Moon makes all of it emotional. Your circle can carry the weight family carries in other charts, and sometimes it replaces family outright. You feel safe when you belong: a team, a congregation, a crew that still meets every year. Your hopes have faces in them, and a goal shared with friends gets finished where a solo one stalls. The group's mood can become your mood, though, so when the circle cracks, your floor goes with it. The group photo from twenty years ago is still on your wall, and you can name everyone in it.",
  "MOON_H12": "Tradition was hard on a 12th house Moon. The house of hidden things and private sorrows was rough on any planet, and the old readings were gloomy. The lived version is gentler and stranger.\n\nYour feelings are vast and mostly offstage, sensed before they're understood. They show up in dreams, in music, in sudden tears at a commercial that had no business doing that. Solitude restores you, and so does water. Your family story may hold something unspoken, a grief nobody named, and you likely picked up on it long before anyone explained. From the outside you look calm. Sometimes you are; sometimes it's a loneliness nobody noticed, you included. Either way, people tell you things they've never told anyone, and you keep every secret.",
  "MOON_H2": "The pantry is full. Not because anyone's hungry, but because a full pantry means things are going to be okay. That's your Moon in one picture.\n\nYou store your sense of safety in things: money in the bank, food in the cupboard, the good sheets, the coat you've had since college. Your belongings carry memory; your grandmother's ring isn't jewelry, it's her. Your spending moves with your mood, and you may earn through work that feeds, houses or comforts people. It's a sensible way to live, until the balance starts standing in for the feeling it was meant to protect. Then no amount feels like enough, and the spare room fills with backups of backups.",
  "MOON_H3": "The Moon was happiest in the 3rd house in the oldest scheme, which called it the house of the Goddess. Short trips, siblings, neighbors, letters, daily talk: the Moon moves fast, and this is the house of moving around.\n\nThat's why your feelings like to travel too. You sort them out in conversation: a call on the drive home, a long text thread with a sister, twenty minutes at the mailbox with a neighbor. A brother or sister may carry more emotional weight for you than either parent did, and school days stay vivid well into middle age. The one step you tend to skip is sitting with a feeling before you talk about it. Naming an emotion and feeling it aren't the same thing.",
  "MOON_H4": "The smell of one particular kitchen sits somewhere near the center of your life. This is the Moon's own house in the natural order: Cancer is the 4th sign, the Moon rules Cancer, and the 4th is home, family, roots and the ground under everything.\n\nYour inner life is built out of where you came from. Your mother, or whoever did the mothering, is right in the middle of the story, along with family recipes, old photos and the house that got sold and still turns up in your dreams. If your early home was good, it anchors you for life. If it wasn't, your long project is building one from scratch, and you probably will, with real care, then fill it with people who needed one too. Home is where you're most yourself and least willing to compromise.",
  "MOON_H5": "What does joy feel like when it's emotional and not just fun? You mostly know the answer.\n\nYour feelings pour into play, romance, children and anything made by hand. A crush becomes an event; a creative project becomes a relationship, with good days and sulky ones. Kids gravitate toward you at family gatherings, because some part of you never stopped playing and they can tell. Your own children, if you have them, are likely your deepest attachment. Your tender spot is the response. A heart this open wants the feeling to land, and when the room doesn't give it back, joy can turn into an audition. Somewhere in a closet is a box of your old drawings, and you still can't throw any of it away.",
  "MOON_H6": "Stress goes to your stomach first. Your body tends to register a feeling before your mind does, and your mind tends to deal with it by cleaning something.\n\nRoutine soothes you. A good day is one that went to plan: kitchen wiped, email answered, squeaky hinge finally oiled. You show care through service, as the coworker who remembers birthdays or the friend who shows up with soup without asking. You may work in health, food or caretaking, and you're very good at it. A to do list does make a handy hiding place, though, and a feeling filed under \"later\" usually waits for a sick day to collect. Put your inner life on the schedule like everything else, not just whatever's left at 11 p.m.",
  "MOON_H7": "Watch yourself in a conversation and you'll catch your face starting to match the other person's. That mirroring is your Moon in the 7th, the house of the partner, whoever's across the table.\n\nYou look for emotional security in a bond. When the relationship is good, everything is good; when it wobbles, your whole inner weather changes. Your partners tend to nurture you or need nurturing, and the roles can swap over a long marriage. You're a natural counselor, host and negotiator. Marriage probably matters to you more than you'd admit on a first date. The work of a lifetime is keeping enough steadiness of your own that another person's mood stops setting yours.",
  "MOON_H8": "You feel everything and show almost none of it.\n\nThe 8th house holds intimacy, trust, death, debt, inheritance and the money that gets tangled up with love, and your Moon puts your emotional life down in that basement. Your feelings run deep and private; you extend trust slowly and withdraw it fast. Grief doesn't frighten you, so people call you when something terrible happens. Your family history may be heavy: a secret, an early loss, a fight nobody brings up at holidays. Control is how you stay safe: read the room, hold the cards, never need anyone too much. It works until intimacy asks you to show your hand. Closeness, for you, is a decision, and once you make it, you're an extraordinary partner.",
  "MOON_H9": "Some people feel homesick abroad. You may feel more at home there.\n\nThe 9th is the house of long journeys, foreign places, belief, higher learning and the search for meaning. You feel safe when life adds up: a faith, a philosophy, a field of study, a teacher whose voice still shows up in your head decades later. A wider horizon soothes your restlessness, which is why you might live far from where you started, or marry into a family nothing like your own. Be careful about mistaking motion for peace. Not every restless feeling is solved by leaving, and a belief system can be a lovely place to avoid feelings that need dealing with closer to home.",
  "NEPTUNE_H1": "Photographs never quite catch you. Friends say the face in the picture looks like someone else's, and in a way they're right. Neptune in the 1st blurs the edges of the self.\n\nThe 1st is your face and your first impression, and Neptune gives it a soft focus. You come across gentle, dreamy, a little hard to pin down. People project onto you: a stranger decides you're an artist, a healer, a kindred spirit, and you often play along without meaning to. You also soak up other people's moods and crowded rooms faster than most. Knowing where you end and someone else begins can take years. Acting, music, photography and any work built on imagination suit you. At some point a total stranger has asked whether you two have met before.",
  "NEPTUNE_H10": "The public sees whatever it wants to see in you. Neptune in the 10th turns your reputation into a screen, and people project onto it.\n\nYour career leans toward the arts, film, music, photography, fashion, ministry, healing or charity, fields where image and inspiration matter. You may find a calling more than a career. Or you drift for years, unsure what you're meant to do, then fall into the right thing almost by accident. A parent may have been idealized, absent or hard to read, and that colors how you deal with authority. A public image can slip out of your control, and a reputation built on glamour can dissolve over one photograph. Your best work is the work you'd have done for free.",
  "NEPTUNE_H11": "Your friend group includes strays: a musician between apartments, someone starting over, a neighbor's kid who needed somewhere to be on Thursday nights.\n\nNeptune in the 11th brings compassion and idealism to friendship and shared hopes. You collect friends from every walk of life and see the best in all of them, sometimes more than is warranted. Groups devoted to spirituality, the arts, recovery or charity draw you in. Your hopes run large and soft: a community that takes care of everyone, a cause that changes things. Disappointment comes when a friend turns out to be using you, or a group you believed in turns out to be ordinary. You give more than you get back. Even so, the potluck you organize every winter keeps growing, and nobody can remember how it started.",
  "NEPTUNE_H12": "Pisces is the 12th sign, and modern astrology gave it to Neptune, so in the 12th house of solitude, the unconscious and retreat, your Neptune is in home water.\n\nYour inner life is enormous. Your dreams are vivid and sometimes seem to know things. A crowded room can feel like standing in surf, every mood washing in at once. Solitude isn't a luxury for you; it's maintenance. Spiritual practice, music, art or quiet service in places most people would rather not look may call to you. Escape is the risk, whether through sleep, screens or simply disappearing for a while. You usually come back with something to show for it: a song, a sketchbook, a calm nobody can explain.",
  "NEPTUNE_H2": "Where did the money go? For you, that's a sincere question, asked often.\n\nNeptune dissolves the hard edges of the money house. Money slips through your fingers: lent to a friend in trouble, given to a cause, spent on something beautiful that seemed essential at the time. Budgets get made and quietly ignored. Imagination or care can pay your bills: art, music, film, healing work, ministry, anything whose value is hard to put on a spreadsheet. You may not want to think about money at all, as if caring would spoil something, and that leaves you open to a bad deal or a charming investor. A good bookkeeper is worth more to you than a good stockbroker. Learn that the cheap way if you can.",
  "NEPTUNE_H3": "You remember the dream better than the meeting. Neptune in the 3rd puts imagination in the house of daily thinking, talk, siblings and school, and your everyday mind has a pleasant fog over it.\n\nSchool could go either way: daydreaming through math, then writing a poem the English teacher still remembers. You think in images and hunches more than lists, and you pick up what people mean more than what they say, which makes you a good listener and an unreliable note taker. A sibling may be someone you idealized, worried about or rescued. Directions are a problem; your map app has heard every apology. You take the scenic route by accident and find a café you talk about for years. Writing, songwriting and storytelling come naturally. The exact wording of what was promised does not.",
  "NEPTUNE_H4": "Your childhood home sounds different every time you describe it. Some details are sharp, some are fog, and a few may not have happened quite the way you remember.\n\nNeptune in the 4th brings mist to home and roots. There may have been something unclear about your early home: a parent who was absent or hard to read, a family secret, a move that left the past blurry. Or the opposite: a home so idealized that real life couldn't measure up. Grown up, you want a home that feels like a sanctuary, near water if possible, with soft light and room to drift. Family can bring confusion and deep loyalty at once, and you might be the one looking after a relative nobody else would. Your house fills with art, plants, cats or rescued furniture, and guests say it's the most peaceful room they've sat in all year.",
  "NEPTUNE_H5": "Romance is a movie to you. The lighting is perfect and the score swells.\n\nNeptune in the 5th brings longing and imagination to love, pleasure, creativity and children. You fall fast and completely, often for someone half real and half invented. Unavailable people have a strange appeal, and so do artists, wanderers and anyone who seems to need saving. Your creative gift can be extraordinary: music, painting, film, dance, fiction, anywhere a feeling becomes something people can step inside. With kids you're gentle, imaginative and a little vague about bedtimes. Trouble comes when the movie ends and an actual person is standing there. Your art probably knows more about love than your dating history does.",
  "NEPTUNE_H6": "Your job description blurs. Somehow you're doing three people's work under one title, and nobody wrote any of it down.\n\nWork and routine get Neptune's soft focus. You're drawn to service: nursing, therapy, chaplaincy, care work, animal rescue, the arts. You give generously and can get taken advantage of, staying late for a boss who never noticed or covering a coworker's mistakes. Routine slips away easily, and the planner gets abandoned by February. Your surroundings matter more than you'd think: harsh lights, noise and a tense office wear you down fast. A clear contract helps. So does a workplace that feels kind.",
  "NEPTUNE_H7": "You fell in love with who they could be. That's often your story, and it can take years to see the difference between the partner and the picture.\n\nNeptune brings idealism and fog to partnership and marriage. Your partners may be artists, healers, seekers or people in some kind of trouble that seemed to ask for rescue, and the connection can feel almost mystical. Business partnerships carry the same risk: a vague contract, a trust nobody wrote down. When it goes badly, there's disillusion and a lot of quiet sacrifice nobody asked for. When it goes well, it's one of the tenderest partnerships there is: two people who see the best in each other and occasionally even live up to it.",
  "NEPTUNE_H8": "Money from a partner, an estate or a settlement arrives, and then nobody's quite sure where it went. Neptune in the 8th puts fog over shared money, debt, inheritance and intimacy.\n\nFinancial entanglements need extra care. Joint accounts, vague loans to family, an inheritance with unclear terms: that's where confusion creeps in. A good lawyer and clear paperwork will save you a lot of grief, and so will reading the whole document before you sign, even the boring middle pages. In intimacy you want to merge completely with someone, which can be beautiful and can also be overwhelming. You're drawn to the spiritual side of life's big changes, and you're a deeply comforting presence when someone's going through the worst of it. Families remember that about you.",
  "NEPTUNE_H9": "Neptune was found on paper before anyone saw it. In 1846, mathematicians worked out where an unseen planet had to be from the way Uranus was being tugged off course, and astronomers pointed a telescope there and found it. Faith in something not yet visible, confirmed: a fitting history for your 9th house Neptune.\n\nReligion, philosophy and far travel are 9th house matters, and Neptune turns them mystical. You're a seeker: pilgrimages, retreats, a teacher or two, a long fascination with poetry or mysticism. Sacred places draw you, and so does life near the sea. The risk is a teacher who promises more than any teacher can deliver, or a belief held because it's beautiful and not because it's true. Your bookshelves hold both kinds, side by side, with pressed flowers marking the pages that mattered.",
  "NORTH_NODE_H1": "Medieval astrologers called the North Node the Dragon's Head and the South Node the Dragon's Tail. They aren't planets; they're the two points where the Moon's path crosses the Sun's, always exactly opposite each other, and modern astrology reads them as a direction of travel: toward the head, away from the tail.\n\nWith the head in your 1st house, you're traveling toward yourself. The tail sits in the 7th, the house of partners, and that's where your old ease lives. Accommodating comes naturally: reading what someone else wants and becoming it. Asking for something for yourself can feel almost rude. So stretch toward a self that exists without an audience. Order first at the restaurant. Pick the movie. Move somewhere because you want to. It feels selfish the first few times. It usually isn't.",
  "NORTH_NODE_H10": "The family needed you, and you were there. With your South Node in the 4th and the North Node opposite in the 10th, that's often the story so far.\n\nHome, family and caretaking feel natural. The public world feels exposed and a little presumptuous, as if wanting a career were a kind of betrayal. Your growth points at exactly that: a public role, a reputation, responsibility outside the house and work with your own name on it. It can come late: the business started after the kids leave, the run for school board, the book finally sent out after twenty years in a drawer. The warmth you learned at home comes with you. It shows up in the way you lead, and the people who work for you notice it on day one.",
  "NORTH_NODE_H11": "Being the center of attention is easy. Being one name on a sign up sheet is harder, and your North Node keeps pointing at the sheet.\n\nYou're coming from the 5th, where your South Node sits, the house of personal creativity, romance and the spotlight. You may have natural flair and a familiar pull toward your own drama, your own projects, your own love story. Your growth runs through friendship, community, collaboration and hopes that belong to more than one person. Coach instead of play. Volunteer where nobody knows your name. Show up to the meeting just to listen. It can feel like dimming the lights. The friends you make this way are the ones still around long after the applause, helping stack the chairs.",
  "NORTH_NODE_H12": "The nodes move backward, sliding through the zodiac in reverse, about eighteen and a half years to go all the way around. Your North Node in the 12th has something of that in it: a direction that asks a busy person to stop pushing forward.\n\nBehind you, in the 6th, your South Node keeps the old habits of work, routine and service. Being useful is your comfort zone; the checklist is safe. Your growth wants rest, solitude, spiritual practice and trust in something you can't control or schedule. An empty afternoon can feel like a real stretch, and so can a retreat with no phone or forgiving yourself for years of overwork. Not everything can be fixed. Some things only get accepted, and that, oddly, is when you start sleeping better.",
  "NORTH_NODE_H2": "Living on someone else's money is comfortable. It's also exactly what your North Node steers you away from.\n\nYour South Node sits opposite in the 8th, the house of shared resources and intimacy, and your familiar pattern runs through merging: a partner's income, family money, joint everything, or relationships so intense they swallow the ordinary business of life. The 2nd points the other way, toward money you earned, things chosen with your own taste and a worth that doesn't depend on anyone else's crisis. It can look modest from outside: a first paycheck that matters more than the inheritance, a savings account in your name, a slow and steady week. The surprise is the calm. Nothing had to be dramatic to be real.",
  "NORTH_NODE_H3": "The big theory can wait. Your North Node points toward the small, the local and the specific, and that's a harder turn than it sounds.\n\nAcross the chart in the 9th is your South Node and everything comfortable about philosophy and far horizons: the grand worldview, the faraway place, the certainty that already knows the answer. Your growth wants curiosity. Questions. Conversations with neighbors who disagree. The sibling you've been meaning to call. A skill learned one lesson at a time instead of read about. You may feel a pull to leave for somewhere bigger, and the growth keeps turning up close to home: a local newsletter, volunteering at the library, learning the names on your block. Listening is a skill like any other, and you get better at it every year.",
  "NORTH_NODE_H4": "Career comes easily. Home is the hard part. That's the usual shape of a 4th house North Node, with the South Node opposite in the 10th.\n\nYou probably know exactly how to perform a public role. Achievement feels familiar and titles feel safe. Your growth points down and inward instead: family, roots, feelings and a home that's actually lived in, not slept in between flights. It can be uncomfortable: turning down the promotion that means moving again, leaving the office at five, learning to cook, finding out what you feel instead of what you've accomplished, and saying it out loud to the people you live with. You may get there in midlife, and the kitchen table ends up being the most important room in the house.",
  "NORTH_NODE_H5": "Somebody has to stand up and sing. With your North Node in the 5th, it's supposed to be you, and you'd almost always rather hand out the lyric sheets.\n\nYour South Node is in the 11th, the house of groups and causes. Belonging comes naturally, and so do blending in, organizing and cheering for other people's talent. Your growth asks for the opposite: personal joy, creative risk, romance, play and the willingness to be the one on stage. Take the solo. Paint something that isn't for anyone. Fall in love without polling your friends first. Play like a kid again on a Saturday. The group doesn't disappear. It becomes your audience for a while, and a generous one.",
  "NORTH_NODE_H6": "Daydreaming is easy. Showing up at eight on Monday is harder, and your North Node points right at Monday.\n\nOpposite it, your South Node sits in the 12th, the house of retreat and solitude, and the old comfort is drifting: sleep, fantasy, a vague sense that things will work out on their own. Your growth is structure: routines, good habits, a craft practiced daily, work that serves someone in a concrete way. It can feel like a loss of magic at first. It isn't. A morning walk, a job done carefully every day for years: these become a spiritual practice of their own. For you, the calendar, of all things, is what finally quiets the mind.",
  "NORTH_NODE_H7": "Doing it alone is your default.\n\nYour South Node in the 1st knows how, and your North Node opposite it, in the 7th, keeps sending a different invitation: do it with someone. Self reliance to a fault is probably how you started: deciding alone, fixing alone, carrying problems alone because asking felt weak. Your direction is cooperation, compromise and real partnership. That means consulting someone before booking the trip, sharing credit on the project, letting a partner's opinion actually change the plan. It can feel like losing a piece of yourself. Usually it adds one. Your best partnerships may come later in life, after the stubbornness softens a few degrees.",
  "NORTH_NODE_H8": "Eclipses only happen near the nodes: a new or full Moon has to fall close to one of these two points for the Sun or Moon to go dark. That's why astrologers treat the nodes as places of sudden change, and in your 8th house, change is the subject.\n\nYour South Node sits opposite in the 2nd, the house of possessions and personal comfort, and your familiar pattern is holding on: to things, to routines, to a self sufficiency that keeps everyone at arm's length. Your growth runs toward merging, shared money, deep intimacy and letting something end so something else can start. So the stretch is trust: a joint account, a partner who sees the whole picture, grief allowed to happen, honesty that goes past the comfortable parts. Very little of it can be planned, which is more or less the point.",
  "NORTH_NODE_H9": "In Indian astrology the nodes are Rahu and Ketu, the head and body of a demon cut in two. Rahu, the head, hungers for what it hasn't had. In your 9th house, what it hasn't had is the big picture.\n\nKetu, your South Node, lands in the 3rd, the house of daily talk, facts and errands. Busy minds live there, gathering information without stepping back far enough to see what it adds up to. Your growth asks for meaning: philosophy, faith, higher learning, travel far enough to unsettle something. That might be the semester abroad finally taken at forty, a degree finished late, a pilgrimage, a philosophy studied seriously instead of skimmed. It means trusting a conviction before every fact is in. Put the phone in a drawer for a week, and something larger comes into focus.",
  "PLUTO_H1": "Rooms go a little quiet when you walk in. Not because you're loud, usually the opposite, but because there's a sense of weight, of someone paying very close attention.\n\nPluto in the 1st concentrates itself in your face and your first impression. Your gaze is direct, sometimes uncomfortably so. People feel seen through, and they react with trust or with wariness, rarely anything in between. You may have gone through something early that changed you for good, a moment when childhood ended ahead of schedule. You'll reinvent yourself more than once. You at forty may look and sound almost nothing like you at twenty, with a clean break in between: a move, a new start, a new name. Old acquaintances need a second to place your face.",
  "PLUTO_H10": "Astronomers demoted Pluto to a dwarf planet in 2006. Astrologers kept using it anyway, and in your 10th house of career and public standing, it's hard to call it minor.\n\nYour ambition runs deep and quiet. You want real power, not just a title, and it usually comes slowly, through strategy and endurance. Politics, finance, law and running large institutions are familiar territory. A parent may have been powerful, controlling or the center of some family drama, and authority stays a charged subject for you. Your reputation can go through dramatic rises and falls, and a career may end completely and restart in a different field. The comebacks are as big as the falls, and your second career is often the one people remember.",
  "PLUTO_H11": "Your friendships are for life or they're over, rarely anything in between.\n\nPluto in the 11th usually comes with a small, fiercely loyal circle and a sharp sense of who is and isn't trustworthy. Groups can be a place of power for you: you might quietly run the board without holding the title, or reform an organization from the inside. Movements and causes that aim to change things at the root attract you. Power struggles inside groups happen, and a friend's betrayal can be a defining wound; a friendship can end abruptly, with no second conversation. Your hopes are big and slow, the kind that take decades, and you're willing to put in the decades.",
  "PLUTO_H12": "Some secrets get kept so well that even the keeper loses track. Your Pluto puts power and depth in the house of hidden things, solitude and the unconscious.\n\nThere's a private intensity in you that rarely shows: fears, habits or family history you don't talk about, a sense of something powerful moving under the surface of your own mind. You may be drawn to psychology, therapy, research or work in the places most people avoid. Solitude is where your real change happens. You're uncannily good at sensing hidden motives in other people. Your own, less so: a friend can read you faster than you can read yourself, which is either a relief or deeply annoying. Therapy, journaling or a long spiritual practice is usually where you finally meet yourself, and it's rarely a quick introduction.",
  "PLUTO_H2": "Money is never just money to you. It's safety, power, proof, and once in a while a weapon.\n\nWith Pluto in the 2nd, your finances go through dramatic cycles: built up, lost, rebuilt, maybe several times. You can be shrewd with resources and good at spotting value where others see junk, and finance, investment, salvage or turning around failing businesses can suit you. You may hold money tightly because you remember exactly what it felt like not to have any. Your possessions carry an emotional charge: some are very hard to let go of, and then one weekend you purge everything and start over. Your self worth gets tested through loss, and each time it comes back stronger. You can probably name your checking balance to the dollar.",
  "PLUTO_H3": "Every word you choose is chosen. Some of them are loaded.\n\nPluto in the 3rd brings depth and force to thinking, talking, siblings and early schooling. Your mind is penetrating. You want to know what's really being said, what's being hidden and what the other person meant by that pause. Research, investigation, psychology and journalism come naturally, and so does the one sentence that ends an argument. Siblings may have been the setting for early power struggles, or for a family secret one of you carried. Conversations with you rarely stay on the surface. Small talk at a party can turn, within ten minutes, into someone's whole life story, and you're never quite sure how it happened.",
  "PLUTO_H4": "What happened in that house mostly stays in that house. Pluto in the 4th puts power, secrets and transformation in the house of home and roots, and your early home may have carried something intense under the surface: a powerful parent, a hidden crisis, a family story told one way in public and another at the kitchen table.\n\nYour relationship with the past is fierce. You might spend years digging through it, in genealogy or in long talks with an aging relative who finally tells the truth. Or you cut ties and build something entirely new. Your adult home goes through dramatic renovation, sometimes literally down to the studs, and real estate can be a source of power for you. There's usually one room, a basement, a workshop, a closet, that nobody else is allowed to rearrange.",
  "PLUTO_H5": "Pluto got its name from an eleven year old schoolgirl in Oxford, in 1930. That's a nice irony for the planet of power and the underworld, and in your 5th house of children, play and creativity, the irony continues. The playground gets intense.\n\nYour love affairs are all consuming. Attraction is magnetic, sometimes obsessive, and breakups can feel like the end of the world. Your creative work is driven, often dark or deeply personal, the kind of art made because not making it isn't an option. Hobbies turn into obsessions: a casual interest in birds becomes a life list of six hundred species. Children, yours or other people's, can bring some of the most transforming experiences of your life. When you love something, you love it completely, and everyone around you hears about it.",
  "PLUTO_H6": "You'll rebuild the whole system rather than patch it. Your work life gets Pluto's full force.\n\nOn the job you're relentless. You see what's broken in a process and won't rest until it's fixed, which makes you invaluable and, to some coworkers, a little frightening. Power struggles at work are common, especially with a boss who doesn't like being questioned. Research, crisis work and anything that demands total focus fit you well. Your habits tend to change all at once, not gradually: one day you overhaul your whole routine and never look back. Given a reason, you can remake your daily life from the ground up.",
  "PLUTO_H7": "Your relationships change you, completely, more than once.\n\nPluto brings power to the house of marriage, partnership and contracts. You attract powerful partners: magnetic, strong willed, sometimes controlling. Your relationships are rarely casual, and attraction quickly turns into something with real stakes. Power is the central question: who leads, who follows, who needs whom more. Some relationships become battles. Others become the most transforming bond of your life, two people who strip each other down to the truth and stay. Therapy, negotiation and mediation suit you, because you can sense what sits under any agreement. You know what the other side really wants, usually before they do.",
  "PLUTO_H8": "Pluto rules Scorpio (Mars is the traditional ruler), and Scorpio is the 8th sign, so your Pluto is on its own ground in the house of intimacy, debt, inheritance and other people's money. It goes all the way down.\n\nThe dark parts of life rarely scare you. Crisis, loss and taboo subjects interest you more than they frighten you, and you've likely come through something big that changed you. Psychology, investigation and any work that goes to the root draw on this placement. Your private life runs deep and stays private. Shared money can be the site of serious power struggles, and you play those fights well, sometimes too well. Your trust is rare and never casual. In a crisis, people feel calmer with you in the room.",
  "PLUTO_H9": "A conversion, in one direction or another. A 9th house Pluto tends to bring at least one moment when a belief system breaks open and gets replaced.\n\nYour faith is never lukewarm. Belief comes in full strength or gets thrown out in full strength, and you may do both over a lifetime. You dig into philosophy and theology the way other people dig into crime novels, looking for what's really going on underneath. Travel can transform you: the trip that changed everything, or the country you ended up living in for a decade. Watch for fanaticism of either kind, the believer who can't stand doubt or the skeptic who can't stand faith. Teach, and you'll make people rethink everything. You may change your mind about the same big question three times before fifty.",
  "SATURN_H1": "Old at twelve, young at sixty. That's the arc a 1st house Saturn tends to draw.\n\nThe 1st is the body, the face and the first impression, and Saturn adds weight. You come across serious, reserved and a little watchful. You were probably called mature as a kid, or handed responsibility early: a younger sibling to watch, a parent who leaned on you. Aries, the 1st sign, is where Saturn falls, and the old picture of a slow planet in a fast place fits how it feels, like a brake on at the start of things. Shyness and self consciousness can take decades to wear off. The payoff comes in the long run. Life often gets easier in your thirties, and by the fiftieth reunion you look better than most of the class.",
  "SATURN_H10": "Capricorn is the 10th sign and Saturn rules it, so in the house of career and public standing your Saturn is on home ground. It builds slowly: Saturn takes about twenty nine and a half years to circle the zodiac, and careers like yours often run on that clock.\n\nThe early years are a climb: a difficult boss, a demanding parent whose standards became the job description, a start that went nowhere. But the reputation you build is solid, based on competence, not flash, and you could finish in charge of something old and serious that nobody else could run. Your weak spot is work becoming the only thing people know you for, and the only thing you know yourself for. You may never fully retire, and keep a desk somewhere well into your eighties.",
  "SATURN_H11": "Three friends, maybe four. That's usually your list, and every one of them has been on it for thirty years.\n\nYour Saturn brings caution to the 11th house, the place for friends and the future you hope for. Fitting in may have been hard when you were young; the lunch table didn't have a seat, or you felt older than everyone. So your friendships form slowly, often with older people or through work, and they last. You keep the club's books, chair the committee and show up to the February meeting when it's ten degrees out and six people came. Your hopes run realistic, sometimes too realistic, scaled back before they're tried because disappointment feels worse than not hoping. The goals you do set, you usually reach, on a schedule you built yourself.",
  "SATURN_H12": "The ancients gave Saturn its joy in the 12th house. That house was called Bad Spirit, the house of confinement and hidden troubles, and it went to the planet of limits and solitude. Saturn, apparently, liked the dark.\n\nYou may carry a private load that never quite shows: fears that arrived early and stayed, a family sorrow nobody explained, a sense of responsibility for something that wasn't yours. Solitude doesn't frighten you, and you may do serious work alone, in archives, labs or night shifts, anywhere quiet and disciplined. You're your own harshest judge, and old guilt can loop for years. Your strength is real, though, and it's the kind built out of sight: patience, endurance, the ability to sit with a hard thing as long as it takes. You might keep a journal for decades that almost nobody gets to read.",
  "SATURN_H2": "Every receipt is in a folder. The folder is labeled, and the label has the year on it.\n\nSaturn in the 2nd brings caution to money, possessions and self worth, and it probably started early. You may have grown up with scarcity, or with a parent who worried about money out loud. You save before you spend, buy the used car and keep it for fifteen years. Your income builds slowly through steady work and often ends up larger than anyone would have guessed. Your self worth works the same way, earned in small deposits, and a compliment gets checked for hidden conditions. Money spent on yourself can sting in a way money spent on others doesn't. Your retirement accounts are probably fine. Feeling secure enough to enjoy them is the real project.",
  "SATURN_H3": "You rewrite the email four times before sending it. Then you check it again after it's sent.\n\nSaturn in the 3rd puts weight on words, learning, siblings and the everyday traffic of the near world. School may have been hard at first, or just serious: a strict teacher, a sense of being slower than the quick kids. What came out of it is a careful, thorough mind that doesn't trust a fact until it's checked. Your writing is precise, and your speech can be slow, dry and funnier than it first appears. A sibling may have been a responsibility more than a playmate, or there may be distance between you. You plan short trips to the minute, and your grocery list is organized by aisle.",
  "SATURN_H4": "Your childhood had rules. Sometimes they were fair, sometimes they weren't, and sometimes the main rule was not to talk about the rules.\n\nSaturn in the 4th puts weight on where you come from. Your early home may have been stable but not soft, or run by a parent who was strict, absent or carrying too much to be fully present. Family responsibility tends to arrive early and stay late. And yet you may build the most solid home of anyone you know. You buy property carefully and hold it. The mortgage gets paid off early, the furnace gets serviced every October, the roof gets replaced before it leaks, and the spare key is exactly where it's supposed to be.",
  "SATURN_H5": "Fun is something you had to learn, and once you learned it, you took it seriously.\n\nThe 5th covers play, romance, children, creativity and pleasure, and your Saturn is the chaperone. Childhood play may have been cut short, or a creative streak waved off as impractical. Romance starts slowly for you, with long caution and a fear of looking foolish, and you may have married or had kids later than your friends, or poured that energy into students, nieces and nephews or a craft. Your creativity is the disciplined kind: the pianist who practices scales for thirty years, the woodworker whose joints are invisible, the comedian who's rewritten the same bit ninety times. It looks effortless to an audience. It's the opposite.",
  "SATURN_H6": "The work gets done, usually by you, usually after everyone else has gone home.\n\nSaturn in the 6th brings duty and endurance to the job and the daily routine. You're the reliable one: never missed a deadline, worked the same unit for twenty two years. Systems make sense to you, and you notice when the safety check gets skipped. Bosses trust you, though reliability is easy to take for granted, so you aren't always the one promoted. Routine suits you and you're good at it. Watch the habit of grinding through when you should stop, and the quiet resentment toward coworkers who don't. Your stamina is real. So is your right to a day off.",
  "SATURN_H7": "Your wedding may come later than the family expected, and when it comes, it's for keeps.\n\nLibra, the 7th sign, is where Saturn is exalted: the slow, serious planet doing well in the sign of fairness and contracts. Something of that carries into your 7th house. You take commitment seriously and want the vows to mean something. Your partners are often older, more established or simply steadier, and a relationship may start as a working partnership before it becomes anything else. What scares you is getting it wrong: an engagement that stretches for years, or the loneliness of feeling you carry the relationship alone. By the fortieth anniversary, though, you're often the couple everyone else quietly measures against.",
  "SATURN_H8": "Somebody has to be the executor. In a lot of families, that's you.\n\nThe 8th covers debt, inheritance, taxes, shared money and intimacy, and Saturn brings seriousness to all of it. A hard stretch early in life may have left you with a lasting respect for how fragile things are. Debt makes you uneasy. You read the fine print, keep the insurance current and had a will before most of your friends thought about one. Intimacy comes slowly; you extend trust in installments, and letting someone see the soft parts can feel like a risk not worth taking. What grows instead is steady competence in the places other people avoid: estates, grief, the conversation nobody wants to have. You're good in that room.",
  "SATURN_H9": "What does a skeptic believe in? You may spend a lifetime answering.\n\nThe 9th covers religion, philosophy, higher education, law and long journeys, and Saturn makes your beliefs earned, not inherited. You may have grown up in a strict faith and argued with it for years, or come to belief late and carefully, after reading everything. Education matters to you and may come with obstacles: money, timing, a degree finished at forty. Your travel has a purpose: the research trip, the posting abroad. You'd make a good teacher of hard subjects, and law or academia may suit you. Watch your worldview hardening into the only acceptable one. At your best, you're the professor who still says \"I don't know\" in front of a full lecture hall, and means it.",
  "SUN_H1": "Being seen is the easy part for you. The hard part is being anything other than what people saw first. They take one look and decide: the confident one, the bright one, the one who walks in like the room was expecting you. That first read can stick for decades, long after you've outgrown it.\n\nNone of it is fake. There's very little distance between your inside and your outside, and that honesty is the best thing about you. But a presence this immediate rarely gets a second impression, so you can spend years living up to the early verdict or quietly arguing with it. Your later chapters get good when you let people be surprised by you.",
  "SUN_H10": "Odds are you were born in the late morning, with the Sun climbing toward the top of the sky, the most visible point a chart has. The 10th is career, reputation and public standing, and there's no more public place to put the Sun.\n\nYour ambition is usually plain to see, and it's less about money than about mattering: a title with your own name on it, a body of work people can point to. The drive often traces back to a parent, usually the more demanding one, whose approval was hard to win. The cost comes when the role becomes the only room in the house. A firing, a retirement or a career that peaked early can feel less like a job change than a loss of self. Plenty of people with your placement are back as consultants within the year.",
  "SUN_H11": "In the group photo you're never in the middle, and somehow everyone is turned a little toward you anyway. The oldest astrologers called the 11th Good Spirit: friends, networks, alliances and the hopes you share with other people.\n\nYou come into focus among many. The team, the band, the congregation, the group chat that's been running since 2009. You're an organizer and a connector, the one who introduces the right two people at the right party, and friends may carry the weight that family carries in other charts. The risk runs opposite to the 10th house: instead of the role swallowing you, you can fade into the group by degrees, agreeing, belonging. The fix is plain: say your real opinion out loud at the meeting where it costs something.",
  "SUN_H12": "Here's the odd thing about your Sun. At your birth it had usually just risen, up in the first couple of hours after sunrise, and yet it sat in the house tradition called Bad Spirit: the hidden house of retreat and things done out of sight.\n\nSo the light is up, and nobody's looking. You probably have a full inner life very few people see, and you do your best work behind the scenes: research, caregiving, art made at 2 a.m. for no audience at all. Recognition comes late, or sideways, or in a form you didn't expect. You may be at peace with that, or you may spend years mixing up being unseen with being nobody. They're not the same thing. Your name may end up in the acknowledgments instead of on the cover, and you may like it there.",
  "SUN_H2": "What are you worth? Most charts get to leave that question in the abstract. Yours doesn't. The Sun in the 2nd ties your sense of self to something you can count: a paycheck, a savings balance, a toolbox, a well built thing with your name scratched on the bottom.\n\nYou probably liked earning your own money early, you'd rather own one good coat than four cheap ones, and you feel most like yourself around things you made or bought with your own effort. Generosity comes easier once the floor is solid. The risk is that a bad year at work feels like a verdict on you instead of on the account. What age tends to bring is a worth that doesn't move when the numbers do.",
  "SUN_H3": "In the oldest scheme the 3rd house belonged to the Moon, and the Sun's favorite spot was across the chart in the 9th, out where the long journeys and big ideas live. So your Sun is the far light parked in the near place: the neighborhood instead of the pilgrimage.\n\nIt usually works beautifully. You come alive in talk, errands, the local news, the sibling who was your first rival and first audience. You think out loud, learn by explaining, and know which café has the good bread. A curious mind keeps you young. What you might miss is your 9th house side, the one that would go deep on one subject for ten years. When it shows up, usually in midlife, it surprises everyone, you included.",
  "SUN_H4": "Your birth time was probably late evening, the couple of hours before midnight, when the Sun sits near the bottom of the sky. The 4th is that underground: home, family, roots, the private floor everything else stands on.\n\nSo your light points inward. The real you shows up at the kitchen table more than at the office, and the parent who ran the household, or the family story itself, sits closer to the center of who you are than anyone outside would guess. You may spend years making peace with the home you were handed, or build, late, the one you always meant to have. Your strength is real; it just doesn't advertise. People find out what you're made of in a crisis, when your foundation holds and the flashier people wobble.",
  "SUN_H5": "A kid's birthday party. Somebody has to run the games, keep the music going and make the shy kid laugh. You're probably already doing it.\n\nThis is the Sun's own territory. Leo belongs to the 5th in the natural order, and the house covers play, romance, children and anything made just for the joy of making it. Your life gets organized around delight. The garage band that never got signed matters. The garden matters. A love affair conducted with real style matters a great deal. One quiet question sits under all of it: is the joy for the making, or for the applause? From across the room they look the same. Only you can tell them apart, and the good years run on the first one.",
  "SUN_H6": "The oldest astrologers called the 6th house Bad Fortune: illness, servitude, work done for someone else. Rough neighborhood for the planet of the self.\n\nModern astrology turned that around, and your Sun shows why. You build yourself through craft, not spotlight. You're the one who understands how the system actually runs, fixes what nobody noticed was broken, and gets named when someone asks who really keeps the place going. Your health and mood track your work closely; a bad stretch on the job shows up in your body first. The old reading still has a point: a self built entirely on being useful can wear thin. Burnout here isn't laziness catching up. It's devotion with no off switch, so treat rest as part of the job.",
  "SUN_H7": "Late afternoon is the likely hour you arrived, the Sun sliding toward the western horizon, the point in the chart that stands for the other person. The 7th holds partners, spouses, collaborators and open rivals: whoever sits across the table.\n\nYou come into focus in company. You warm up in conversation, sharpen in a negotiation, and often find out what you believe by hearing what someone else believes first. Your partners tend to be strong, bright, a little larger than life, which feels like a gift in one decade and like standing in their light the next. It isn't just that relationships matter to you. You get assembled inside them, and a partner's name tends to come up in the first five minutes of any conversation with you.",
  "SUN_H8": "Some people get through a crisis. Some people get built by one. You're usually the second kind.\n\nThe 8th house holds what polite conversation steps around: death, debt, inheritance, sex, other people's money, the shared stuff a family fights over. You form yourself in exactly that territory. You're often the one people call when something terrible happens, because you don't flinch and you don't need it explained. You give away very little about yourself; trust comes slowly, and once broken it rarely comes back. Power and secrets interest you for the same reason: you want to know what's really running the room. The danger is mistaking control for safety.",
  "SUN_H9": "By the old count this is the Sun's happiest house. The oldest astrologers gave it the 9th and called the house God, and it covers what a sunny life reaches for: meaning, faith, long journeys, higher learning, law and books.\n\nYou build yourself around a search. A degree that turned into a calling. A faith joined, left, or argued with for forty years. A year abroad that rearranged everything. You're frank, a little restless, and probably holding a book you want to lend someone. Teachers changed your life, and you may end up teaching. The trap is the horizon that keeps moving: the next idea, the next country, the next certainty. Keep at least one old friend who argues with you, and keep inviting them to dinner.",
  "URANUS_H1": "Uranus spins on its side, its axis tipped so far over that it more or less rolls around the Sun. You may give a similar impression: something about you is set at an angle to everyone else.\n\nThe 1st is your body, your face and the way you walk into a room, and Uranus puts the unexpected right there. Your haircut changes every year. Your clothes don't quite match the occasion, on purpose. You say the thing nobody else at the table was going to say, and you get bored of each version of yourself right around the time other people get used to it. You may have been called weird as a kid and decided early to take it as a compliment. Restlessness is the cost. Plans get dropped mid stride, and the people closest to you learn to expect the sudden turn. They do expect it. They still get surprised.",
  "URANUS_H10": "Career changes, plural. A 10th house Uranus rarely follows one ladder all the way up.\n\nYour working life runs on the unexpected. Jobs end suddenly and new ones appear just as fast. You may work in a field that didn't exist when you started, or invent a role nobody had thought of. Technology, science, media, activism and self employment suit you. Authority has been a sore point since a particular gym teacher in seventh grade, and bosses who demand obedience don't last long in your life. You're likely to become the boss who lets people work however they want. Some of your best career moves will look like mistakes for about five years. Your résumé, when you bother to update it, reads like three different people.",
  "URANUS_H11": "Aquarius is the 11th sign, and modern astrology made Uranus its ruler, so your Uranus is on its own modern ground in the house of friends, groups and the future.\n\nYour friends are many, mixed and a little unusual. The circle might include a physicist, a tattoo artist and someone you met in a forum about obscure synthesizers. Groups devoted to reform, technology, science or causes ahead of their time attract you, and you're often the one with the strange idea that turns out, ten years later, to be the obvious one. Closeness can be harder than friendliness. You show up for the group while keeping some distance from any one person, and friendships can end as suddenly as they began. Your hopes involve the whole world more than one house with a fence. Some of them even come true.",
  "URANUS_H12": "Ideas arrive at three in the morning, fully formed, from somewhere you can't quite locate. Your Uranus puts sudden insight in the house of the unconscious, solitude and the hidden.\n\nYour rebellion is private. On the outside you can look entirely conventional, quiet job and tidy yard, while your inner life runs on strange dreams, intuitions and radical opinions you rarely share. Breakthroughs come through solitude, meditation, therapy or a long walk alone, and one sudden experience may have that rearranged everything. A jolt of nerves can arrive in an empty room for no obvious reason. Writing it down helps. So does finding the one or two people who can hear your strange ideas without flinching. Keep them for life.",
  "URANUS_H2": "Your income chart may look like a heart monitor: big months, flat months, a windfall, a surprise bill, a job that ended without warning and a better one three weeks later.\n\nYour Uranus makes money the least predictable thing in your life. You may earn in unusual ways: freelancing, technology, inventions, side businesses, a career that didn't exist when you were in school. A steady paycheck can feel like a cage. Your values are independent, and what you own says so, whether it's a vintage synthesizer, a camper van or a firm lack of interest in owning much at all. Security is the tricky part: a temperament that thrives on change has a hard time with thirty year mortgages. Then again, your best investment may be the strange one everyone told you to skip.",
  "URANUS_H3": "Who teaches themselves a programming language at fourteen, mostly to prove a teacher wrong? You, possibly. Your mind runs fast, sideways and in bursts, and the 3rd is the house of thinking, talking, learning and the neighborhood.\n\nSchool was complicated, either boring or behind you, and a lot of your real education came from the library and the internet. Ideas arrive as flashes, often mid conversation, and you can jump three topics before anyone catches up. Your siblings may be unusual or far away: a brother across the world, a half sister you didn't meet until adulthood. Your writing is original and sometimes hard to follow. You change your mind often and say so cheerfully, which drives the people who quoted you last week a little crazy.",
  "URANUS_H4": "Moving boxes. Lots of them, maybe across a childhood with several addresses, a sudden divorce or a household that ran on rules no other family on the street used.\n\nUranus in the 4th brings disruption to home and roots. Your early home was likely unusual somehow: an unconventional parent, a military family, furniture rearranged every season. As an adult you want freedom at home more than comfort. You might live in a converted bus, a renovated church, a different city every few years, or a normal looking house with a very strange basement. Your roots are complicated. You may build a chosen family, or keep going back to make sense of where you came from. A permanent address sounds better in theory than it turns out in practice.",
  "URANUS_H5": "Love at first sight, then gone by spring.\n\nUranus in the 5th brings surprise to romance, creativity, pleasure and children. Attraction hits you suddenly, often toward someone unexpected: a different age, a different background, someone your family would never have guessed. Relationships built on freedom suit you better than ones built on routine. Creativity is where this placement shines. Your art is original, sometimes experimental, often ahead of its audience: electronic music, odd sculpture, a comedy act half the room gets. As a parent you'd be more friend than drill sergeant. The thrill of the new thing fades fast, and you're already looking for the next one. Or you find one person interesting enough to keep surprising you for forty years.",
  "URANUS_H6": "The nine to five was invented by someone else, and you've been trying to get out of it since the first week.\n\nUranus in the 6th brings restlessness to work and routine. Repetitive jobs drain you fast. You do best with flexible hours, remote work, contract gigs or jobs built on technology and problem solving, where finding a better way gets rewarded instead of punished. Coworkers find you refreshing or exhausting, sometimes in the same afternoon. You're the one who automated half the department, then got bored and started on the parking schedule. Stress shows up as jittery energy and odd hours. A little routine helps, and you resist it the way a cat resists a bath.",
  "URANUS_H7": "The wedding was at the courthouse on a Tuesday, or in a forest, or not at all. You handle partnership on your own terms.\n\nUranus brings independence and surprise to the house of marriage. Your partners are often unusual: brilliant, eccentric, much older or younger, from a very different world. Attraction is sudden. Your relationships need room to breathe, and setups that look odd from outside, like separate houses or long distance, may work fine for you. Stability is the hard part. Partnerships can start or end abruptly, and the urge for freedom can arrive in the middle of a perfectly good marriage. Find someone just as independent as you are, and you'll be the most interesting couple at any dinner party.",
  "URANUS_H8": "Sudden money, sudden loss, sudden change of heart. Uranus in the 8th puts the unpredictable planet in the house of shared resources, inheritance, debt and intimacy, so the deepest parts of your life tend to arrive without warning.\n\nAn inheritance from a relative you barely knew. A partner's business that folded overnight. One phone call that rearranged everything. You've lived through enough upheaval to develop a strange calm about it. In intimacy you're frank and experimental, and you need some freedom even in your closest bonds. Taboo subjects fascinate you, along with psychology and astrology, the things other people only whisper about. Your investments can swing wildly, and a sensible emergency fund may be the most rebellious thing you ever do.",
  "URANUS_H9": "Uranus was the first planet found with a telescope, in 1781, and astrologers came to link it with revolution, invention and sudden insight. In your 9th house of belief, philosophy, learning and long journeys, those land on the big questions.\n\nWhatever you were taught gets questioned. A religious upbringing gets examined and often set aside, and unusual philosophies, fringe science and radical politics draw you in. Your education may be unconventional: dropped out, went back, self taught, three degrees in unrelated fields. You travel spontaneously: a one way ticket, a plan changed at the airport, a month somewhere you couldn't have found on a map a year ago. You can be a visionary teacher or an exhausting dinner guest, depending on the evening. A belief you hold today may be gone next year, replaced by something stranger, explained with exactly the same confidence.",
  "VENUS_H1": "Strangers hold the door for you. Waiters remember your order. Your Venus puts something pleasing right on the surface: your face, your voice, the way you arrive. People respond before they could say why.\n\nIt's often more manner than looks. You make an awkward moment easier without seeming to try, you probably dress with some care, and people have told you your whole life that you're easy to be around. That's a real gift, and also a quiet job, because being liked can turn into a role, and the role starts making decisions: the yes said to keep things smooth, the honest sentence swallowed. You may spend your twenties finding out whether people like you or like the ease. Usually it's both, and the later version of you is just as warm, only on purpose.",
  "VENUS_H10": "Likability is a career asset, and Venus at the top of your chart gives you plenty. The 10th is the house of career and reputation, and people generally enjoy working with you, from the boss to the client to the public.\n\nYour career may run through beauty, art, fashion, design, diplomacy or hospitality, or it may be an ordinary job where your personal touch made the difference. Love and work can overlap: a business started with a spouse, a partner who opened the right door. Your public image is usually polished. Image management can become the whole job, though, if staying liked means dodging hard decisions. Midcareer often hands you a choice between being liked and being respected. Pick respect, and you usually end up with both.",
  "VENUS_H11": "Friends who became lovers, and lovers who stayed friends: your Venus makes friendship the main language of love.\n\nThe 11th covers friends, groups and the hopes you share with others. You're well liked in groups and good at gathering them, and your place is where everybody ends up. You host, you introduce, you remember who's feuding with whom and seat them at opposite ends of the table. Groups devoted to art, causes or simply good times tend to find you. A wide circle can stand in for closeness: lots of friends, not many who really know you, and a hard week shows the difference. The richer version keeps both: the party, and the two or three people who stay afterward to help with the dishes.",
  "VENUS_H12": "Venus never strays far from the Sun. When the Sun was still below the horizon at your birth, a 12th house Venus was the morning star, already up and shining before anyone was awake. That's a fair picture of your love: real, bright and mostly unwitnessed.\n\nThe 12th is the house of hidden things, solitude and retreat, and your feelings run deep and private here: secret crushes, quiet devotions, a love you never fully talked about. Your compassion is strong, and you may be drawn to help people in hard places that the world overlooks. Art and music can feel almost sacred to you. Be careful with love as sacrifice: giving too much, loving someone unavailable, keeping a relationship hidden because hidden feels safer. There may be a love letter in a drawer somewhere, never sent, kept anyway.",
  "VENUS_H2": "Why buy the cheap one twice? You tend to know better.\n\nTaurus is the 2nd sign and Venus rules Taurus, so your Venus is at home in the house of money, possessions and values. Your taste is good and often expensive: good fabric, good food, the well made chair that will outlive you. Money may come to you through beauty or pleasure, such as design, art, food, hospitality or simply being pleasant to do business with. And you actually enjoy what you have, which is rarer than it sounds. Comfort can turn into medicine, though: shopping after a bad day, keeping things because letting go feels like loss. With age, you enjoy beautiful things without needing them to prove anything.",
  "VENUS_H3": "You may be one of the last people still sending handwritten thank you notes. The 3rd house is the near world of talk, letters, siblings, neighbors and short trips, and your Venus makes all of it more gracious.\n\nYou're easy to talk to. You can phrase a hard thing kindly, make small talk feel like it matters and write a note someone keeps in a drawer for years. Your siblings likely matter to you, and the neighbors like you. Teaching, writing, sales and anything that runs on friendly communication suit you. When a conversation turns tense, though, you smooth it over, and charm can talk its way around the real problem. You're probably the one who writes the sympathy card everyone else signs.",
  "VENUS_H4": "Peace at home matters to you more than almost anything. Venus in the house of home, family and roots wants a home that's beautiful and calm and full of people who love each other, and if you weren't born into one, you'll spend a lifetime building it.\n\nSo your house gets attention: the paint color, the table set properly, the garden, the guest room that's always ready. Home is where you recharge and where you're most loving. There may be a parent who made home feel safe, and a lifelong soft spot for the place you grew up. Later life often brings the home you always pictured. Your risk is peace at any price: keeping things nice can mean never saying what's wrong, and harmony can quietly become silence. The best homes you build can hold a real argument and still feel like home.",
  "VENUS_H5": "The oldest astrologers named the 5th house Good Fortune and said Venus was happiest there. Romance, pleasure, play, creativity, children: if any planet was going to love a house, it was this one in this one.\n\nRomance is an art form for you: flowers, good restaurants, conversations that run past midnight. You may have real creative talent, especially for anything with beauty or performance in it, and people remember your parties. Kids adore you. What happens when the fun part ends? The chase can get more attention than the relationship, and commitment can feel at first like the party winding down. You can go deep; you just have to want to, and the wanting can take a while. When the anniversary parties come, they're spectacular.",
  "VENUS_H6": "Virgo is the 6th sign, and Virgo is where Venus falls. A house doesn't carry dignity the way a sign does, but the echo is there: the planet of pleasure lands in the house of chores, routine and work done for someone else.\n\nIt often makes you the one who makes the workplace bearable. You remember the birthday cake, smooth over the fight between departments and bring a plant for the desk nobody bothered with. Your work may involve beauty, care or comfort: design, wellness, hospitality, nursing, anything that helps people feel better. Romance can start at work. Your body responds to small pleasures; good food, good sleep and a pleasant routine do wonders for you. The weak spot is putting up with too much: unpaid hours, a bad boss who's nice in person, a schedule that suits everyone but you. Your kindness is real. The boundaries have to be learned.",
  "VENUS_H7": "You give the best toasts at weddings. This is Venus in its own territory: Libra is the 7th sign, Venus rules Libra, and the 7th is partnership, marriage and the art of getting along with one other person.\n\nYou're a relationship person. You're good at compromise, good at reading what a partner needs and often good at choosing someone who brings grace, money or social ease. Business partnerships and negotiations tend to go well, because you can calm a room and close a deal with the same smile. Your hazard is losing track of what you want: the yes said to keep the peace, the partner who looks right on paper, the relationship kept going because ending it would be unpleasant. Your best partnerships come after you've learned to be a whole person on your own.",
  "VENUS_H8": "Surface affection doesn't count with you.\n\nThe 8th house is the deep end of the chart: intimacy, sex, shared money, debt, inheritance and the changes that remake a person. Your Venus wants love that goes all the way down. Your relationships tend to be all or nothing, intensely private and sometimes a little dangerous in their pull. Money may arrive through other people: a partner's income, an inheritance, investments, a business built on shared resources. You see beauty where others look away, in grief, in mystery, in the parts of people usually kept hidden. Watch for love turning into control, jealousy or keeping score. Trust is your turning point, and when it comes, you're as loyal as anyone alive.",
  "VENUS_H9": "You fall in love with cities. Venus in the house of long journeys, foreign places, philosophy and belief falls for the wider world.\n\nA partner from another culture, a romance that started on a trip, a philosophy that feels beautiful as much as true: that's your pattern. Travel lights you up, especially the slow kind with no fixed return date, and so do art, literature and languages. You're open minded, generous about other people's beliefs and good company in a debate, because you actually enjoy the other side's argument. The tension is the grass on the other side of the ocean: the next country, the next teacher, an ideal love waiting somewhere else, while the real thing gets passed over. Your kitchen probably has spices from four countries and a story about each one."
}
